1
00:00:04,571 --> 00:00:05,638
TOKYO-HAKONE EKIDEN RACE

2
00:00:05,705 --> 00:00:06,873
The Hakone Ekiden.

3
00:00:07,507 --> 00:00:12,245
Its official name is the Tokyo-Hakone
Round-Trip College Ekiden Race.

4
00:00:12,312 --> 00:00:17,183
Founded in 1920,
it is the longest relay race

5
00:00:17,250 --> 00:00:19,152
in college long-distance running.

6
00:00:19,219 --> 00:00:23,523
Only 21 teams can compete.

7
00:00:23,590 --> 00:00:26,659
The top ten teams
with automatic qualification,

8
00:00:26,726 --> 00:00:31,798
ten teams that clear the qualifying race,
and the Kanto Student United Team.

9
00:00:32,732 --> 00:00:35,735
Each school passes down its uniform

10
00:00:35,802 --> 00:00:39,272
and the sash linking history and passion.

11
00:00:39,939 --> 00:00:43,843
As the new year dawns,
a story unfolds of young runners,

12
00:00:44,611 --> 00:00:46,980
locked in a fierce battle,
their souls throwing off sparks.

13
00:00:56,589 --> 00:01:00,860
BASED ON THE NOVEL
ORETACHI NO HAKONE EKIDEN BY JUN IKEIDO

14
00:01:03,563 --> 00:01:05,365
KOKUSHIKAN UNIVERSITY
TAKUSHOKU UNIVERSITY

15
00:01:10,770 --> 00:01:15,909
TOKYO-HAKONE ROUND-TRIP
COLLEGE EKIDEN QUALIFYING RACE

16
00:01:27,120 --> 00:01:29,656
Mr. Tokushige,
less than one minute to air!

17
00:01:29,722 --> 00:01:31,024
I know!

18
00:01:33,560 --> 00:01:34,761
Thirty seconds to air!

19
00:01:36,162 --> 00:01:37,263
Made it!

20
00:01:37,797 --> 00:01:42,302
For Dainichi TV's Maradona,
I've gotten pretty rusty.

21
00:01:42,368 --> 00:01:43,470
A hundred meters max.

22
00:01:43,536 --> 00:01:46,406
-Twenty seconds to air!
-Bureau Chief Kitamura's been on my case.

23
00:01:46,473 --> 00:01:47,841
Video segment is cued.

24
00:01:47,907 --> 00:01:50,076
Nice shot on Camera One!

25
00:01:50,143 --> 00:01:51,311
-Mr. Tokushige.
-Huh?

26
00:01:51,377 --> 00:01:54,247
-Please be quiet for a moment.
-Okay.

27
00:01:54,314 --> 00:01:57,016
Opening video segment,
Mr. Maeda, give us the opening call.

28
00:01:57,083 --> 00:02:00,153
Copy that. Opening video in 20 seconds.
Thank you.

29
00:02:00,220 --> 00:02:02,122
-Ten seconds to air!
-Okay.

30
00:02:02,188 --> 00:02:05,992
-Nine, eight, seven, six…
-Here's the latest weather.

31
00:02:06,059 --> 00:02:10,730
-Five seconds! Four, three, two, one.
-Roll the video segment!

32
00:02:10,797 --> 00:02:11,865
MIYAKO FOR HAKONE EKIDEN

33
00:02:16,603 --> 00:02:19,005
HAKONE EKIDEN
QUALIFYING RACE

34
00:02:19,939 --> 00:02:22,041
After the video segment,
we'll open wide on the start.

35
00:02:22,108 --> 00:02:25,411
-Yes.
-Close on the runners. Cameras, stand by.

36
00:02:25,478 --> 00:02:28,014
-Five seconds!
-Four, three…

37
00:02:28,081 --> 00:02:30,416
‎-two, one.
‎-Camera one, go!

38
00:02:30,984 --> 00:02:31,784
At last,

39
00:02:31,851 --> 00:02:35,755
the time has come to fight
for a spot in the Hakone Ekiden.

40
00:02:35,822 --> 00:02:36,990
For their school's honor

41
00:02:37,056 --> 00:02:39,459
and for their own futures,

42
00:02:39,526 --> 00:02:41,794
-a battle for every single second begins.
-Go to the rules.

43
00:02:41,861 --> 00:02:44,330
Forty-two schools have entered.

44
00:02:44,397 --> 00:02:46,499
Each team can field up to 12 runners,

45
00:02:46,566 --> 00:02:47,800
and the top ten times determine

46
00:02:47,867 --> 00:02:49,536
-the standings.
-Show the lineup graphic.

47
00:02:49,602 --> 00:02:52,739
Ten schools will earn
a ticket to the main race.

48
00:02:58,878 --> 00:03:00,613
Let's go over the plan again.

49
00:03:00,680 --> 00:03:01,514
Yes, sir.

50
00:03:01,581 --> 00:03:02,549
MEISEI MANAGER - KEITO YANO

51
00:03:02,615 --> 00:03:05,185
Meisei, gather up! Strategy check!

52
00:03:05,251 --> 00:03:06,252
-Yes!
-Yes!

53
00:03:08,588 --> 00:03:11,591
Yusuke and I will run in the lead pack
and battle the other top runners.

54
00:03:11,658 --> 00:03:12,492
CAPTAIN - HAYATO AOBA

55
00:03:12,559 --> 00:03:15,395
The rest of you,
form the second pack around Kengo!

56
00:03:15,461 --> 00:03:16,462
-Yes!
-Yes!

57
00:03:16,529 --> 00:03:17,897
Everyone runs for everyone.

58
00:03:17,964 --> 00:03:20,600
Shave off every second you can.

59
00:03:21,367 --> 00:03:24,070
-Yusuke and I will lead the way.
-Yes!

60
00:03:24,637 --> 00:03:27,207
All ten of us, under ten hours
and 35 minutes total!

61
00:03:28,174 --> 00:03:29,209
Let's do this!

62
00:03:29,809 --> 00:03:30,677
-Yeah!
-Yeah!

63
00:03:31,611 --> 00:03:32,478
Coach.

64
00:03:38,284 --> 00:03:41,354
You can do this.

65
00:03:42,722 --> 00:03:43,590
Got it?

66
00:03:44,557 --> 00:03:46,292
Go and seize Hakone!

67
00:03:46,359 --> 00:03:47,393
-Yes!
-Yes!

68
00:03:48,494 --> 00:03:49,562
All right, huddle up!

69
00:03:53,199 --> 00:03:56,102
-Let's go!
-Yeah!

70
00:03:57,136 --> 00:03:58,304
Keep Meisei on screen.

71
00:03:58,871 --> 00:04:00,640
This is their year.

72
00:04:00,707 --> 00:04:03,509
Leading Meisei Gakuin University
is the legendary Coach Moroya.

73
00:04:03,576 --> 00:04:05,645
Close-up on the head coach.
Okay, on-screen graphics.

74
00:04:05,712 --> 00:04:07,513
After heartbreak the last two years,

75
00:04:07,580 --> 00:04:09,415
they’re back at Hakone after three years.

76
00:04:09,983 --> 00:04:11,084
Commentator, Mr. Daigo.

77
00:04:11,150 --> 00:04:14,621
The once-fearsome coach looks calm today.

78
00:04:14,687 --> 00:04:16,122
Yes.

79
00:04:16,189 --> 00:04:18,992
If Meisei Gakuin's two top runners
run to their ability,

80
00:04:19,058 --> 00:04:20,293
I think they could place high.

81
00:04:20,360 --> 00:04:21,561
-Mr. Hara.
-Yes?

82
00:04:21,628 --> 00:04:22,495
The qualifying race

83
00:04:22,562 --> 00:04:25,265
has a different kind of tension.

84
00:04:25,331 --> 00:04:28,134
Because the ten runners' total time
determines the result.

85
00:04:28,201 --> 00:04:29,936
One great runner isn't enough.

86
00:04:30,003 --> 00:04:32,605
-Every step matters.
-Camera Two!

87
00:04:32,672 --> 00:04:37,043
You never know how a race
will turn out until the very end.

88
00:04:37,677 --> 00:04:39,178
There's a monster lurking.

89
00:04:39,846 --> 00:04:40,780
Right.

90
00:04:40,847 --> 00:04:43,850
The pressure at the Hakone
qualifying race is enormous.

91
00:04:43,916 --> 00:04:46,286
Anything can happen.

92
00:04:47,987 --> 00:04:50,657
A total of 504 runners

93
00:04:50,723 --> 00:04:53,860
now line up on the 45-meter-wide runway.

94
00:04:53,926 --> 00:04:56,362
The start is moments away.

95
00:04:59,966 --> 00:05:02,535
Thirty seconds to the start.

96
00:05:06,272 --> 00:05:07,106
Hayato.

97
00:05:10,176 --> 00:05:11,644
This is our last chance.

98
00:05:14,080 --> 00:05:15,048
We're going to Hakone.

99
00:05:15,114 --> 00:05:16,516
MEISEI GAKUIN UNIVERSITY

100
00:05:16,582 --> 00:05:17,583
Yeah.

101
00:05:20,286 --> 00:05:22,422
Ten seconds to the start!

102
00:05:22,955 --> 00:05:24,624
Camera Three, pan after the start.

103
00:05:24,691 --> 00:05:25,958
Then go to Car One.

104
00:05:26,025 --> 00:05:27,627
Come on.

105
00:05:28,194 --> 00:05:28,995
On your marks.

106
00:05:34,100 --> 00:05:35,902
And they're off!

107
00:05:36,703 --> 00:05:41,341
The fierce race
for a place in Hakone has begun!

108
00:05:44,377 --> 00:05:45,978
Car One, go.

109
00:05:47,980 --> 00:05:49,482
After this, we go to the course intro.

110
00:05:49,549 --> 00:05:50,683
Copy that.

111
00:05:50,750 --> 00:05:52,952
Three, two,…

112
00:05:53,019 --> 00:05:55,321
one, start.

113
00:05:55,388 --> 00:05:59,192
The course is a half marathon.
21.0975 kilometers.

114
00:05:59,258 --> 00:06:02,028
Runners start at Japan Ground Self-Defense
Force Camp Tachikawa

115
00:06:02,095 --> 00:06:03,663
and do about three laps of the runway.

116
00:06:04,197 --> 00:06:06,799
Then they head into town,
and just before 14 kilometers,

117
00:06:06,866 --> 00:06:09,335
the stage shifts to Showa Kinen Park.

118
00:06:10,036 --> 00:06:14,474
Every year, one second can decide fate.

119
00:06:14,540 --> 00:06:16,676
That's the Hakone Ekiden qualifying race.

120
00:06:16,743 --> 00:06:19,846
Maeda's commentary really
pulls it all together.

121
00:06:19,912 --> 00:06:21,948
Hakone is in good hands.

122
00:06:23,182 --> 00:06:26,152
The international runners
have passed ten kilometers.

123
00:06:26,219 --> 00:06:29,155
At ten kilometers,
a large Japanese pack is led by

124
00:06:29,222 --> 00:06:31,858
Meisei Gakuin's two top runners.

125
00:06:32,992 --> 00:06:35,928
The race has moved into Showa Kinen Park.

126
00:06:35,995 --> 00:06:39,799
And here comes Kenta Morimoto
of Juntendo University!

127
00:06:44,704 --> 00:06:47,840
From the first pack,
Kenta Morimoto of Juntendo…

128
00:06:47,907 --> 00:06:49,809
Hayato is looking good so far.

129
00:06:50,476 --> 00:06:52,612
At this rate, he'll beat the 1:03 target.

130
00:06:55,081 --> 00:06:55,948
Here they come.

131
00:06:56,516 --> 00:06:59,051
Come on, Hayato! Come on, Yusuke!

132
00:06:59,118 --> 00:07:00,853
Good pace!

133
00:07:00,920 --> 00:07:02,054
Come on!

134
00:07:05,458 --> 00:07:09,595
Hayato Aoba of Meisei Gakuin
is running strong.

135
00:07:09,662 --> 00:07:12,899
Aoba missed the qualifying race

136
00:07:12,965 --> 00:07:14,801
the last two years because of injuries.

137
00:07:14,867 --> 00:07:17,403
He must be determined
to make it count this time.

138
00:07:17,970 --> 00:07:19,839
-There's Meisei. I knew it.
-Now Meisei's Aoba

139
00:07:19,906 --> 00:07:21,274
-Aoba. Caption.
-draws level

140
00:07:21,340 --> 00:07:22,842
with Juntendo's Morimoto!

141
00:07:22,909 --> 00:07:23,743
You got it!

142
00:07:23,810 --> 00:07:26,012
Will Aoba make his move here?

143
00:07:29,682 --> 00:07:30,750
You got it!

144
00:07:32,485 --> 00:07:34,887
MEISEI GAKUIN UNIVERSITY
HAKONE EKIDEN QUALIFYING RACE

145
00:07:45,832 --> 00:07:48,801
Oh, he's holding his side.
Hayato Aoba of Meisei Gakuin

146
00:07:49,469 --> 00:07:50,903
-looks strained.
-Is he okay?

147
00:07:50,970 --> 00:07:52,638
Stay on Aoba a little longer.

148
00:07:52,705 --> 00:07:56,008
Could that be a side stitch?

149
00:07:56,075 --> 00:07:57,643
It can happen when you're running well.

150
00:07:57,710 --> 00:07:59,045
Zoom out a little.

151
00:07:59,979 --> 00:08:02,615
Now Morimoto of Juntendo University
moves back in front!

152
00:08:02,682 --> 00:08:03,549
KENTA MORIMOTO

153
00:08:04,550 --> 00:08:06,786
Will Juntendo University

154
00:08:06,853 --> 00:08:09,121
safely qualify?

155
00:08:09,188 --> 00:08:11,524
-Hayato!
-Meisei Gakuin

156
00:08:11,591 --> 00:08:13,426
may have a problem.

157
00:08:13,926 --> 00:08:16,596
I'm worried about Captain Aoba.

158
00:08:20,166 --> 00:08:21,300
-Come on!
-You can do it!

159
00:08:23,135 --> 00:08:24,504
-Come on!
-You can do it!

160
00:08:24,570 --> 00:08:26,405
-Come on!
-You can do it!

161
00:08:33,446 --> 00:08:36,015
Here is the turnaround at 17.4 kilometers.

162
00:08:36,082 --> 00:08:38,017
-Yusuke's on track for a personal best!
-Mr. Daigo.

163
00:08:38,084 --> 00:08:41,287
What should runners watch for
at this turnaround?

164
00:08:41,354 --> 00:08:42,922
We're already late in the race.

165
00:08:42,989 --> 00:08:45,658
Hayato is 20 seconds behind his target.

166
00:08:45,725 --> 00:08:47,927
And they also need to avoid…

167
00:08:49,529 --> 00:08:51,130
The runners behind…

168
00:08:51,197 --> 00:08:53,132
Hold that shot.

169
00:08:53,199 --> 00:08:54,967
-Showing on-screen graphics.
-That's Shibata

170
00:08:55,034 --> 00:08:56,669
and Onishi of Nihon University.

171
00:08:56,736 --> 00:08:59,205
And three from Senshu University too!

172
00:08:59,272 --> 00:09:01,541
Everyone's making their move now!

173
00:09:01,607 --> 00:09:04,677
The final three kilometers
are the hardest in a half marathon.

174
00:09:05,411 --> 00:09:08,114
Digging deep here
will make all the difference!

175
00:09:08,180 --> 00:09:10,550
The schools are starting to make moves.

176
00:09:10,616 --> 00:09:11,584
Yes.

177
00:09:11,651 --> 00:09:13,786
-Hayato…
-Meisei Gakuin's Hayato Aoba

178
00:09:13,853 --> 00:09:15,054
looks like he's struggling.

179
00:09:15,621 --> 00:09:17,657
Less than two kilometers remain.

180
00:09:17,723 --> 00:09:20,726
For a short stretch,
there won't be any fans along the course.

181
00:09:28,801 --> 00:09:30,503
Yusuke and I will lead the way!

182
00:09:30,570 --> 00:09:31,737
We're going to Hakone.

183
00:09:31,804 --> 00:09:35,074
You can do this.

184
00:09:35,141 --> 00:09:36,842
Go and seize Hakone!

185
00:09:49,155 --> 00:09:51,357
Is Aoba picking up the pace again?

186
00:09:51,424 --> 00:09:52,758
Meisei Gakuin's Aoba…

187
00:09:52,825 --> 00:09:54,360
-Put up Meisei's caption.
-Oh.

188
00:09:54,427 --> 00:09:55,962
He passes one runner here.

189
00:09:56,028 --> 00:09:58,798
-Center on Meisei and follow him.
-He's giving everything he has

190
00:09:58,864 --> 00:10:01,000
to shave off one second.

191
00:10:06,038 --> 00:10:08,474
That's the captain's pride.

192
00:10:08,541 --> 00:10:10,076
-Captain Aoba
-Hayato, you can do it!

193
00:10:10,142 --> 00:10:12,712
gives everything to this final push.

194
00:10:13,312 --> 00:10:16,415
Can Meisei Gakuin, the old powerhouse,
make a comeback?

195
00:10:16,482 --> 00:10:18,150
Stay on Aoba's expression.

196
00:10:18,217 --> 00:10:20,386
He's giving it his all!

197
00:10:20,453 --> 00:10:21,587
Hayato Aoba!

198
00:10:39,138 --> 00:10:41,674
Runners are finishing one after another.

199
00:10:41,741 --> 00:10:44,310
They're shaving off every second they can!

200
00:10:44,377 --> 00:10:45,878
They're pumping their arms.

201
00:10:55,888 --> 00:10:59,325
Hakone is decided by the combined
time of each team's top ten runners.

202
00:10:59,392 --> 00:11:00,626
Yusuke!

203
00:11:01,360 --> 00:11:03,796
-Great run!
-Great run!

204
00:11:03,863 --> 00:11:05,498
-Great run!
-Where is Hayato?

205
00:11:07,299 --> 00:11:08,668
We're in the closing stages.

206
00:11:08,734 --> 00:11:09,735
Hayato!

207
00:11:09,802 --> 00:11:11,404
He's giving

208
00:11:11,470 --> 00:11:12,638
it everything he has.

209
00:11:12,705 --> 00:11:13,539
-Let's go!
-One second

210
00:11:13,606 --> 00:11:15,374
-You got it!
-here could decide

211
00:11:15,441 --> 00:11:17,877
-whether they qualify for Hakone.
-You got it!

212
00:11:20,946 --> 00:11:24,417
TOKYO-HAKONE ROUND-TRIP
COLLEGE EKIDEN QUALIFYING RACE

213
00:11:28,788 --> 00:11:29,922
Are you okay?

214
00:11:29,989 --> 00:11:31,891
-Can you stand?
-Can you stand?

215
00:11:31,957 --> 00:11:33,559
-Let's move.
-Yeah.

216
00:11:35,761 --> 00:11:38,664
NUMBER, NAME, GOAL TIME

217
00:11:39,365 --> 00:11:40,533
These schools have already…

218
00:11:40,599 --> 00:11:42,001
-How is it?
-Yes.

219
00:11:42,068 --> 00:11:43,335
They've crossed the finish line.

220
00:11:43,402 --> 00:11:47,406
But this only means
their top ten runners have finished.

221
00:11:47,473 --> 00:11:49,108
These are not the official standings.

222
00:11:49,608 --> 00:11:51,544
Great job, Hayato!

223
00:11:51,610 --> 00:11:52,478
My time?

224
00:11:55,014 --> 00:11:57,349
YUSUKE-ONE HOUR, TWO MINUTES, TEN SECONDS
HAYATO-ONE HOUR, THREE MINUTES, 24 SECONDS

225
00:12:04,190 --> 00:12:05,524
It's okay, Hayato.

226
00:12:06,225 --> 00:12:08,728
Yusuke set a personal best
and made up a lot of time.

227
00:12:10,963 --> 00:12:12,098
I'm sure we made it!

228
00:12:18,104 --> 00:12:21,307
The results will be announced shortly.

229
00:12:22,942 --> 00:12:26,712
The top ten schools from
the last Hakone Ekiden are already seeded.

230
00:12:26,779 --> 00:12:29,582
They automatically qualify next year.

231
00:12:29,648 --> 00:12:32,518
Forty-two teams
entered this qualifying race.

232
00:12:32,585 --> 00:12:35,855
Only ten will run the Hakone Ekiden.

233
00:12:36,422 --> 00:12:37,323
Will they make it?

234
00:12:43,262 --> 00:12:44,597
The results are coming up shortly.

235
00:12:44,663 --> 00:12:47,500
Stay on Meisei, Toho Economics and Senshu.

236
00:12:47,566 --> 00:12:49,835
Hakone Ekiden qualifying race…

237
00:12:49,902 --> 00:12:53,339
Only ten schools from this field
will earn the right to run Hakone.

238
00:12:56,809 --> 00:12:59,278
TOKYO-HAKONE ROUND-TRIP
COLLEGE EKIDEN QUALIFYING RACE

239
00:13:02,648 --> 00:13:06,018
We will now announce the results
of the qualifying race

240
00:13:06,085 --> 00:13:10,089
for the Tokyo-Hakone
Round-Trip College Ekiden Race.

241
00:13:11,123 --> 00:13:12,057
In first place…

242
00:13:12,124 --> 00:13:13,159
PLACE, UNIVERSITY, TIME

243
00:13:13,225 --> 00:13:14,527
Juntendo University,

244
00:13:14,593 --> 00:13:17,763
-10 hours, 33 minutes, 23 seconds.
-Attention! Bow!

245
00:13:17,830 --> 00:13:19,165
Thank you!

246
00:13:19,732 --> 00:13:22,568
Second place is Nihon University…

247
00:13:22,635 --> 00:13:24,336
Take Nichidai.

248
00:13:24,403 --> 00:13:26,772
Nihon University takes second place.

249
00:13:28,574 --> 00:13:32,111
Sixth place,
Nippon Sport Science University,

250
00:13:32,178 --> 00:13:35,447
10 hours, 36 minutes, 7 seconds.

251
00:13:36,015 --> 00:13:37,149
Seventh place,

252
00:13:38,784 --> 00:13:40,953
Yamanashi Gakuin University,

253
00:13:41,020 --> 00:13:43,789
10 hours, 37 minutes, 15 seconds.

254
00:13:43,856 --> 00:13:45,057
There's still a chance.

255
00:13:47,860 --> 00:13:51,630
Only three Hakone berths remain.

256
00:13:52,364 --> 00:13:55,201
Eighth place, Hosei University,

257
00:13:55,267 --> 00:13:57,236
-Okay, Hosei caption.
-10 hours, 37 minutes.

258
00:13:57,303 --> 00:13:59,872
-It's Hosei University. Two remain.
-21 seconds…

259
00:14:03,509 --> 00:14:04,610
Ninth place…

260
00:14:07,313 --> 00:14:10,182
Takushoku University,
10 hours, 37 minutes…

261
00:14:10,249 --> 00:14:12,952
-On-screen graphics for Takushoku.
-Next is Takushoku University.

262
00:14:13,652 --> 00:14:15,855
Just one school left…

263
00:14:17,756 --> 00:14:19,024
Tenth place…

264
00:14:23,229 --> 00:14:26,198
Meisei… Meisei…

265
00:14:27,633 --> 00:14:28,834
The last school.

266
00:14:32,538 --> 00:14:35,274
Senshu University,
10 hours, 38 minutes, 2 seconds.

267
00:14:35,341 --> 00:14:37,176
-Take Senshu.
-Senshu University claims

268
00:14:37,243 --> 00:14:39,912
the final Hakone berth.

269
00:14:40,479 --> 00:14:44,483
Those are the ten schools
that qualify for the Hakone Ekiden.

270
00:14:49,455 --> 00:14:51,457
-Stay on Meisei and Toho Economics.
-They'll run

271
00:14:51,523 --> 00:14:53,158
-Hakone next year.
-Eleventh place…

272
00:14:54,894 --> 00:14:56,195
Meisei Gakuin University.

273
00:14:58,197 --> 00:15:00,666
Ten hours, 38 minutes, 12 seconds.

274
00:15:02,101 --> 00:15:04,103
By ten seconds.

275
00:15:04,169 --> 00:15:06,705
Unfortunately, Meisei Gakuin University

276
00:15:06,772 --> 00:15:09,875
failed to qualify for the Hakone Ekiden
by ten seconds.

277
00:15:09,942 --> 00:15:12,511
They were only ten seconds
behind Senshu University.

278
00:15:13,345 --> 00:15:16,916
-By ten seconds?
-A world decided by just ten seconds.

279
00:15:17,483 --> 00:15:19,251
-The monster was there after all.
-One second…

280
00:15:19,318 --> 00:15:20,753
Twelfth place…

281
00:15:23,522 --> 00:15:26,258
-Toho University of Economics.
-Twelfth is Toho University of Economics.

282
00:15:33,666 --> 00:15:34,967
Hello, Tokushige speaking.

283
00:15:35,567 --> 00:15:37,937
Where are we on that thing?

284
00:15:40,172 --> 00:15:42,775
Could you give me a little more time?

285
00:15:43,509 --> 00:15:45,110
What are you talking about?

286
00:15:46,011 --> 00:15:48,347
We're less than three months from Hakone.

287
00:15:49,014 --> 00:15:50,115
You get that?

288
00:15:51,984 --> 00:15:52,851
Yes.

289
00:15:53,485 --> 00:15:56,956
Then let me talk to you next week.

290
00:15:57,022 --> 00:15:58,157
Goodbye.

291
00:16:13,639 --> 00:16:14,473
I'm sorry!

292
00:16:17,743 --> 00:16:18,911
I'm sorry, everyone.

293
00:16:20,412 --> 00:16:21,547
It's my fault.

294
00:16:25,718 --> 00:16:27,219
I'm sorry…

295
00:16:32,358 --> 00:16:34,159
Everyone, gather around.

296
00:16:41,834 --> 00:16:45,337
You gave it your best!
You did really well!

297
00:16:48,507 --> 00:16:50,609
You guys gave it everything

298
00:16:51,243 --> 00:16:53,512
this entire year.

299
00:16:57,116 --> 00:16:58,150
But sadly,

300
00:16:59,618 --> 00:17:03,255
the dream didn't come true.

301
00:17:07,693 --> 00:17:11,397
You lost.

302
00:17:15,334 --> 00:17:16,402
But…

303
00:17:17,269 --> 00:17:20,472
it's great losers

304
00:17:21,507 --> 00:17:23,475
who make the winners shine.

305
00:17:26,512 --> 00:17:30,682
Right now, you are great losers.

306
00:17:31,850 --> 00:17:32,851
Starting tomorrow,

307
00:17:33,485 --> 00:17:39,191
run with the goal of
becoming shining winners.

308
00:17:40,559 --> 00:17:42,227
Run with your heads held high.

309
00:17:43,362 --> 00:17:47,533
I'm proud of every one of you.

310
00:17:50,002 --> 00:17:51,370
Thank you.

311
00:17:55,841 --> 00:17:56,775
Hayato.

312
00:17:58,077 --> 00:18:00,679
Hold your head high and stand proud.

313
00:18:28,107 --> 00:18:29,541
SPORTS DEPARTMENT

314
00:18:31,376 --> 00:18:34,379
Five minutes for the qualifying race
segment on the noon news?

315
00:18:34,446 --> 00:18:36,081
-Got it.
-Mr. Tokushige.

316
00:18:36,815 --> 00:18:40,452
That qualifying race was something!
Meisei Gakuin missed by just ten seconds!

317
00:18:40,986 --> 00:18:42,321
It gave me chills.

318
00:18:42,387 --> 00:18:45,557
-Races really are alive.
-Right.

319
00:18:47,726 --> 00:18:49,294
-Um, excuse me.
-Huh?

320
00:18:49,361 --> 00:18:52,498
I'm from a variety show
called Laugh to Death.

321
00:18:52,564 --> 00:18:55,167
-I need clearance to use WBC footage…
-Oh.

322
00:18:55,701 --> 00:18:57,269
For WBC, talk to him.

323
00:18:57,336 --> 00:18:59,304
-Mr. Muroi.
-Yes.

324
00:18:59,371 --> 00:19:01,240
-Him.
-Thank you!

325
00:19:01,907 --> 00:19:03,675
Don't make the players
do anything too stupid!

326
00:19:04,276 --> 00:19:07,179
-Mr. Tokushige, the printout is ready.
-Oh, thank you.

327
00:19:07,246 --> 00:19:10,282
HAKONE EKIDEN REFORM PROPOSAL

328
00:19:12,117 --> 00:19:13,318
HAKONE EKIDEN
STAFF ROOM

329
00:19:13,385 --> 00:19:15,454
Wait, I have to watch all of these?!

330
00:19:15,521 --> 00:19:16,955
Show her how it works.

331
00:19:17,022 --> 00:19:18,323
Okay.

332
00:19:21,927 --> 00:19:23,195
Is it this one?

333
00:19:23,262 --> 00:19:24,229
CONTROL ROOM

334
00:19:24,296 --> 00:19:25,464
Okay.

335
00:19:25,531 --> 00:19:27,633
Zoom in on Car One in the back.

336
00:19:29,301 --> 00:19:33,172
You didn't understand Ms. Miyamoto's
directions at the qualifier, did you?

337
00:19:34,006 --> 00:19:36,542
This includes
the broadcast director's calls

338
00:19:36,608 --> 00:19:37,576
from the main race.

339
00:19:37,643 --> 00:19:39,444
It’ll help you
understand the live workflow,

340
00:19:39,511 --> 00:19:40,746
so watch it and study up.

341
00:19:40,812 --> 00:19:43,549
Still, 20 years of this?

342
00:19:44,249 --> 00:19:46,018
That's 280 hours.

343
00:19:46,084 --> 00:19:47,553
Impossible!

344
00:19:47,619 --> 00:19:50,322
-Hey!
-Good morning!

345
00:19:52,124 --> 00:19:53,692
-Oh, the Director's Voice.
-Yes.

346
00:19:53,759 --> 00:19:55,961
I watched plenty of those.

347
00:19:56,028 --> 00:19:58,230
I recommend 2018.

348
00:19:58,297 --> 00:19:59,631
What happened that year?

349
00:19:59,698 --> 00:20:01,633
That's when
Mr. Tokushige was the broadcast director.

350
00:20:02,768 --> 00:20:05,871
Cool, precise calls. Perfect flow.

351
00:20:05,938 --> 00:20:06,972
It'll give you chills.

352
00:20:07,039 --> 00:20:08,340
Right, Miyamoto?

353
00:20:08,407 --> 00:20:10,509
How long is the qualifying race segment
for noon news?

354
00:20:11,476 --> 00:20:12,578
It's five minutes.

355
00:20:12,644 --> 00:20:15,681
Mr. Nomura, for five minutes,
focus on the Juntendo captain's interview

356
00:20:15,747 --> 00:20:18,217
and Takushoku University's
international runner.

357
00:20:18,283 --> 00:20:19,551
Got it.

358
00:20:19,618 --> 00:20:20,686
-Miyamoto.
-Yes.

359
00:20:20,752 --> 00:20:21,787
Here.

360
00:20:22,621 --> 00:20:25,457
-Mr. Kuwa. Could you all take a look?
-Huh?

361
00:20:25,524 --> 00:20:27,226
Everyone, take a look at this.

362
00:20:28,193 --> 00:20:30,028
"Hakone Ekiden Reform Proposal."

363
00:20:30,095 --> 00:20:32,064
I put it together myself.

364
00:20:32,898 --> 00:20:35,334
Looks good. More cameras too.

365
00:20:35,867 --> 00:20:36,802
It's realistic.

366
00:20:36,868 --> 00:20:39,571
Changes like these are totally fine,

367
00:20:39,638 --> 00:20:41,406
but will Bureau Chief Kuroishi
accept this?

368
00:20:42,007 --> 00:20:43,976
Doesn't he want to turn Hakone
into a variety show?

369
00:20:44,042 --> 00:20:46,044
Kuroishi?

370
00:20:46,111 --> 00:20:47,546
He's a tough opponent.

371
00:20:47,613 --> 00:20:50,382
He's Dainichi TV's very own…

372
00:20:50,449 --> 00:20:51,350
TETSU KUWANA

373
00:20:51,416 --> 00:20:53,318
What was it? That…

374
00:20:53,385 --> 00:20:56,922
-Like that pro wrestler. The De…
-The Destroyer?

375
00:20:56,989 --> 00:20:59,658
-That's it.
-Why do they call him that?

376
00:20:59,725 --> 00:21:02,561
He smashes precedent
and sends the ratings soaring.

377
00:21:02,628 --> 00:21:04,529
That's the so-called Kuroishi Method

378
00:21:04,596 --> 00:21:06,498
that got him to Programming Bureau Chief.

379
00:21:06,565 --> 00:21:08,467
I heard he was the first to cast

380
00:21:08,533 --> 00:21:11,103
a comedian as an info show's main host.

381
00:21:11,169 --> 00:21:13,972
That was when I worked under him.

382
00:21:14,806 --> 00:21:17,509
I heard something the other day.
They've started putting

383
00:21:17,576 --> 00:21:19,044
countdowns on kiss scenes in dramas.

384
00:21:20,012 --> 00:21:21,747
What, like "One minute to the kiss,

385
00:21:21,813 --> 00:21:23,649
59, 58…"? Like that?

386
00:21:23,715 --> 00:21:25,217
Wait, that's so convenient!

387
00:21:26,618 --> 00:21:30,322
Toyama, you totally watch
dramas at double speed.

388
00:21:30,389 --> 00:21:31,723
-How'd you know?
-Well,

389
00:21:31,790 --> 00:21:34,192
results are all that matter.

390
00:21:34,760 --> 00:21:37,029
Maybe countdowns will be normal someday.

391
00:21:38,096 --> 00:21:39,498
I'll upload the script when ready.

392
00:21:39,564 --> 00:21:40,465
Thank you.

393
00:21:40,532 --> 00:21:42,467
-I'll contact them properly later.
-Okay.

394
00:21:43,268 --> 00:21:45,270
-Hashiguchi.
-Yes?

395
00:21:45,337 --> 00:21:47,439
Okay. Let's go grab lunch.

396
00:21:48,407 --> 00:21:51,076
Mr. Tokushige, shouldn't you run

397
00:21:51,143 --> 00:21:52,878
the Hakone proposal
by Bureau Chief Kitamura?

398
00:21:55,013 --> 00:21:57,182
He's been a weathervane lately.

399
00:21:57,249 --> 00:21:59,718
I'm Kitamura. Nice to meet you.

400
00:21:59,785 --> 00:22:02,688
Um… Needless to say,

401
00:22:02,754 --> 00:22:04,556
I'm against it.

402
00:22:05,357 --> 00:22:07,659
Doesn't Mr. Kuroishi just want credit

403
00:22:07,726 --> 00:22:09,828
for having changed something?

404
00:22:10,462 --> 00:22:12,698
I don't sense a shred of respect

405
00:22:12,764 --> 00:22:14,032
for sports broadcasting.

406
00:22:15,901 --> 00:22:18,103
Well, I'll talk to him.

407
00:22:19,004 --> 00:22:19,938
MEISEI GAKUIN UNIVERSITY

408
00:22:20,005 --> 00:22:20,939
TRACK AND FIELD TEAM DORMITORY

409
00:22:21,006 --> 00:22:22,607
HEAD COACH'S OFFICE

410
00:22:23,408 --> 00:22:24,476
Oh, come in.

411
00:22:27,379 --> 00:22:28,447
Excuse me.

412
00:22:32,651 --> 00:22:34,753
-Have a seat.
-Okay.

413
00:22:45,897 --> 00:22:48,800
There's something
I should tell you in advance.

414
00:22:51,436 --> 00:22:52,971
The truth is…

415
00:22:54,806 --> 00:22:57,709
I'm stepping down as head coach.

416
00:22:58,777 --> 00:22:59,611
‎Huh?

417
00:22:59,678 --> 00:23:01,980
I've done enough.

418
00:23:13,058 --> 00:23:14,259
I'm sorry…

419
00:23:19,197 --> 00:23:23,201
The qualifying race result is my fault.

420
00:23:25,704 --> 00:23:27,973
If I hadn't faded there,

421
00:23:30,142 --> 00:23:31,510
we'd surely have made the top ten…

422
00:23:32,677 --> 00:23:35,046
This isn't you guys' fault.

423
00:23:36,915 --> 00:23:41,286
I decided to step down a long time ago.

424
00:23:45,957 --> 00:23:50,429
For a long time, I've watched

425
00:23:50,495 --> 00:23:54,599
you guys more closely than anyone.

426
00:23:54,666 --> 00:23:56,168
That's why I know.

427
00:24:00,372 --> 00:24:01,706
You'll be fine.

428
00:24:02,774 --> 00:24:07,712
You can manage without me.

429
00:24:11,183 --> 00:24:16,021
From here on,
I'll leave things to my successor.

430
00:24:18,790 --> 00:24:19,991
Your successor?

431
00:24:21,860 --> 00:24:23,662
It's already decided.

432
00:24:25,330 --> 00:24:26,731
Who is it?

433
00:24:28,500 --> 00:24:30,368
Masato Kai.

434
00:24:31,770 --> 00:24:32,637
Mr. Kai?

435
00:24:33,171 --> 00:24:35,173
-Masato Kai?
-Yes.

436
00:24:35,240 --> 00:24:38,710
I heard it when I interviewed
a Meisei Gakuin alum recently.

437
00:24:38,777 --> 00:24:41,713
Coach Moroya is retiring
after this season,

438
00:24:41,780 --> 00:24:43,748
and Masato Kai will be the new head coach.

439
00:24:45,150 --> 00:24:47,419
What was his nickname again?

440
00:24:47,486 --> 00:24:49,621
-The "Meisei Express."
-That's it.

441
00:24:49,688 --> 00:24:51,623
Was Mr. Kai really that fast?

442
00:24:51,690 --> 00:24:53,892
He ran the prestigious second leg
from his first year.

443
00:24:53,959 --> 00:24:55,260
I think he's won the leg twice.

444
00:24:55,327 --> 00:24:57,596
He ran leg two all four years
and won it three times.

445
00:24:58,530 --> 00:25:00,165
-Right.
-Didn't he

446
00:25:00,232 --> 00:25:03,502
join a regular company after university?

447
00:25:03,568 --> 00:25:06,037
Yes, a big trading company,
of all things. Uh…

448
00:25:06,104 --> 00:25:07,906
Tohto Chuo Bussan.

449
00:25:09,341 --> 00:25:11,176
Could you be quiet for a bit?

450
00:25:12,744 --> 00:25:15,614
Why would Mr. Kai suddenly come back?

451
00:25:16,748 --> 00:25:20,285
I heard he'd cut all ties with track.

452
00:25:21,586 --> 00:25:23,021
I see.

453
00:25:24,022 --> 00:25:27,058
So Kai's going to be a head coach…

454
00:25:27,125 --> 00:25:30,195
Is Mr. Kai quitting his company?

455
00:25:32,030 --> 00:25:36,101
He's taking a year's leave to come here.

456
00:25:37,068 --> 00:25:38,303
A year…

457
00:25:39,004 --> 00:25:43,008
Starting today, the team sets off

458
00:25:43,842 --> 00:25:46,545
with Kai for the next Hakone.

459
00:25:49,581 --> 00:25:51,883
And Hayato.

460
00:25:52,884 --> 00:25:55,720
You're on the Student United Team.

461
00:25:57,856 --> 00:26:00,458
The Kanto Student United Team

462
00:26:00,525 --> 00:26:03,695
is made up of the top 16 runners
from teams that failed to qualify

463
00:26:03,762 --> 00:26:06,998
for the Hakone Ekiden.

464
00:26:07,065 --> 00:26:10,035
It participates as an
additional 21st team.

465
00:26:10,602 --> 00:26:13,905
It's only open to runners
who have never run the Hakone Ekiden.

466
00:26:13,972 --> 00:26:16,374
It is led by the head coach of the team

467
00:26:16,875 --> 00:26:19,811
that placed 11th

468
00:26:19,878 --> 00:26:21,379
in the qualifying race.

469
00:26:21,446 --> 00:26:23,415
Got it, Hayato?

470
00:26:25,350 --> 00:26:27,118
Earn one of the ten spots

471
00:26:27,953 --> 00:26:30,956
on the Student United Team.

472
00:26:31,923 --> 00:26:32,891
And run Hakone

473
00:26:33,758 --> 00:26:36,528
for the teammates

474
00:26:37,462 --> 00:26:39,064
who couldn't!

475
00:26:42,400 --> 00:26:46,838
So Mr. Moroya ends his career
with the Student United Team?

476
00:26:46,905 --> 00:26:49,307
Apparently Mr. Kai will handle that too.

477
00:26:49,374 --> 00:26:50,942
He said there's no point.

478
00:26:51,509 --> 00:26:53,345
That's one unusual move after another.

479
00:26:53,912 --> 00:26:54,746
Um…

480
00:26:55,680 --> 00:26:57,549
I've always wondered about this.

481
00:26:57,616 --> 00:26:58,883
The Student United Team

482
00:26:58,950 --> 00:27:02,220
gathers top runners from schools
that missed Hakone, right?

483
00:27:02,287 --> 00:27:04,189
So why do they never win?

484
00:27:04,255 --> 00:27:07,158
Other schools live and eat together
365 days a year.

485
00:27:07,225 --> 00:27:10,261
They come together as one.

486
00:27:10,328 --> 00:27:13,231
A team thrown together
after the qualifying race can't beat that.

487
00:27:13,298 --> 00:27:15,133
And no matter how fast they run,

488
00:27:15,200 --> 00:27:17,669
their times don't go on record, right?

489
00:27:17,736 --> 00:27:19,537
They aren't ranked either.

490
00:27:19,604 --> 00:27:21,573
It's a non-scoring entry.

491
00:27:22,240 --> 00:27:26,611
So what motivates them to run?

492
00:27:28,813 --> 00:27:30,548
Because it's Hakone, maybe?

493
00:27:32,150 --> 00:27:33,485
Right.

494
00:27:34,486 --> 00:27:38,123
That's what Hakone is.

495
00:27:40,458 --> 00:27:42,293
As of today,

496
00:27:43,361 --> 00:27:46,431
I'm stepping down
as head coach of this team.

497
00:27:46,498 --> 00:27:47,866
-Huh?
-Huh?

498
00:27:47,932 --> 00:27:50,201
-Huh?
-What? Resigning?

499
00:27:52,837 --> 00:27:56,141
For 38 years,

500
00:27:57,575 --> 00:28:01,079
I yelled at runners
who didn't do as I wished

501
00:28:02,647 --> 00:28:05,150
and made them obey.

502
00:28:07,519 --> 00:28:09,621
I believed

503
00:28:11,156 --> 00:28:13,892
that was my way of coaching.

504
00:28:16,361 --> 00:28:17,195
But…

505
00:28:18,430 --> 00:28:20,832
it seems that was wrong.

506
00:28:21,633 --> 00:28:22,534
No.

507
00:28:24,602 --> 00:28:28,339
It was wrong.

508
00:28:29,641 --> 00:28:30,942
From here on,

509
00:28:32,043 --> 00:28:35,747
I'll entrust the team to a new head coach.

510
00:28:36,581 --> 00:28:39,451
-A new head coach?
-A new head coach?

511
00:28:41,052 --> 00:28:42,520
Let me introduce him.

512
00:28:43,922 --> 00:28:45,657
Your new head coach, Masato Kai.

513
00:28:49,461 --> 00:28:52,464
NEW HEAD COACH OF
MEISEI GAKUIN UNIVERSITY-MASATO KAI

514
00:29:02,707 --> 00:29:05,510
-A few words, please.
-Sure.

515
00:29:10,281 --> 00:29:11,316
I'm Kai.

516
00:29:13,551 --> 00:29:15,386
We're going back to Hakone.

517
00:29:15,453 --> 00:29:17,989
That's my only goal.

518
00:29:19,491 --> 00:29:20,959
To get there,

519
00:29:21,926 --> 00:29:23,795
I'll overhaul
the way things are done if needed.

520
00:29:24,295 --> 00:29:25,663
Overhaul?

521
00:29:29,834 --> 00:29:33,171
Be ready and follow me.

522
00:29:35,740 --> 00:29:36,574
That's all.

523
00:29:54,893 --> 00:29:56,528
Did you know about this?

524
00:29:59,764 --> 00:30:01,833
That Coach Moroya was quitting.

525
00:30:06,638 --> 00:30:07,939
I knew it.

526
00:30:11,276 --> 00:30:14,412
Do you really think Mr. Kai
should be our head coach?

527
00:30:16,915 --> 00:30:17,749
What do you mean?

528
00:30:17,816 --> 00:30:20,351
He's using his company's
social contribution program

529
00:30:20,418 --> 00:30:22,220
to coach us for only one year, right?

530
00:30:22,287 --> 00:30:23,454
So our team's being used

531
00:30:23,521 --> 00:30:26,624
to help his career.

532
00:30:28,259 --> 00:30:29,194
Who told you that?

533
00:30:29,260 --> 00:30:31,629
The Trustee, Ms. Yoneyama.

534
00:30:31,696 --> 00:30:33,765
The alumni association objects, too.

535
00:30:34,632 --> 00:30:37,902
The guys on our team say it's wrong too.

536
00:30:38,903 --> 00:30:40,905
Coach Moroya

537
00:30:40,972 --> 00:30:43,074
was tough, sure.

538
00:30:43,141 --> 00:30:45,810
But everyone looked up to him

539
00:30:45,877 --> 00:30:48,746
because we believed in him!

540
00:30:49,681 --> 00:30:51,950
Can we really make it to Hakone like this?

541
00:30:56,988 --> 00:31:00,024
Well, I guess it doesn't concern you.

542
00:31:02,493 --> 00:31:05,496
You're going to Hakone, right?

543
00:31:08,633 --> 00:31:10,368
With the Student United Team.

544
00:31:11,870 --> 00:31:13,338
He brought it up, didn't he?

545
00:31:14,806 --> 00:31:18,710
I ran Hakone in my first year,
so I'm not eligible anymore.

546
00:31:20,745 --> 00:31:21,613
No.

547
00:31:23,147 --> 00:31:26,050
Nothing's official yet,

548
00:31:26,117 --> 00:31:27,085
-but…
-But?

549
00:31:32,423 --> 00:31:33,591
Good for you, Hayato.

550
00:31:35,526 --> 00:31:37,462
Do your best for all of us.

551
00:31:37,528 --> 00:31:38,963
We'll all be cheering for you.

552
00:32:01,419 --> 00:32:02,654
Hayato!

553
00:32:05,957 --> 00:32:07,025
Thank you.

554
00:32:08,026 --> 00:32:09,727
Don't push yourself too hard.

555
00:32:13,264 --> 00:32:15,433
I can't settle down
unless I'm doing something.

556
00:32:19,270 --> 00:32:23,141
Time will sort things out with Coach Kai.

557
00:32:24,142 --> 00:32:27,011
Everyone just hasn't come
to terms with it yet.

558
00:32:35,086 --> 00:32:36,054
Um…

559
00:32:37,488 --> 00:32:40,158
I'm joining too, as team manager.

560
00:32:42,660 --> 00:32:43,928
The Student United Team.

561
00:32:45,964 --> 00:32:47,198
I'll do my best.

562
00:32:50,702 --> 00:32:51,569
I see…

563
00:32:59,177 --> 00:33:00,144
Hayato,

564
00:33:01,479 --> 00:33:05,917
are you having second thoughts?
About running for the Student United Team?

565
00:33:11,356 --> 00:33:15,860
You missed the qualifying race
the last two years because of injuries.

566
00:33:17,996 --> 00:33:22,066
I think I know how you felt

567
00:33:22,600 --> 00:33:24,435
watching Hakone these two years.

568
00:33:26,838 --> 00:33:30,375
That's why I want you to run.

569
00:33:38,516 --> 00:33:41,119
Should a captain who dragged
the team down at the qualifying race

570
00:33:42,153 --> 00:33:45,823
be allowed to run Hakone?

571
00:33:51,829 --> 00:33:53,598
I was only ten seconds short.

572
00:34:02,540 --> 00:34:04,809
Oh, sorry.

573
00:34:05,576 --> 00:34:06,444
I'm going to bed.

574
00:34:07,712 --> 00:34:08,780
See you tomorrow.

575
00:34:17,054 --> 00:34:21,359
DAINICHI TV PROGRAMMING
BUREAU CHIEF-TAKESHI KUROISHI

576
00:34:23,694 --> 00:34:25,229
HAKONE EKIDEN REFORM PROPOSAL

577
00:34:28,433 --> 00:34:32,170
As for Hakone,

578
00:34:32,236 --> 00:34:36,541
I don't intend to change the basic format.

579
00:34:36,607 --> 00:34:38,209
Think again.

580
00:34:40,611 --> 00:34:43,815
You think repeating the same thing
will bring in more viewers?

581
00:34:45,049 --> 00:34:47,118
If you want better ratings,

582
00:34:47,185 --> 00:34:49,287
come up with a new framework.

583
00:34:49,353 --> 00:34:53,591
Which is why I'd add motorbike cameras

584
00:34:53,658 --> 00:34:55,927
to catch the tactics we've missed--

585
00:34:55,993 --> 00:34:57,161
Impact!

586
00:34:58,496 --> 00:35:01,032
Impact! Impact!

587
00:35:01,999 --> 00:35:03,101
Impact!

588
00:35:04,435 --> 00:35:08,106
What we need is impact like never before!

589
00:35:08,172 --> 00:35:10,441
Stop clinging to the old ways!

590
00:35:10,508 --> 00:35:12,877
-But--
-Those who don't care about sports…

591
00:35:12,944 --> 00:35:15,746
We need ideas that draw in people
like viewers

592
00:35:15,813 --> 00:35:17,348
watching a comedy show instead.

593
00:35:18,449 --> 00:35:20,184
What exactly do you have in mind?

594
00:35:20,885 --> 00:35:22,820
Improve the studio guest lineup.

595
00:35:24,222 --> 00:35:26,424
-That's…
-It's drab.

596
00:35:27,525 --> 00:35:28,693
Boring.

597
00:35:29,727 --> 00:35:33,397
That narrow view of sports coverage
and all that talk about grit.

598
00:35:34,532 --> 00:35:37,735
Guests only Ekiden fans have heard of.

599
00:35:38,503 --> 00:35:40,271
It could use a star or two.

600
00:35:40,972 --> 00:35:44,909
Of course a show needs some glamour.

601
00:35:45,443 --> 00:35:49,013
But Hakone is a serious sports broadcast.

602
00:35:49,881 --> 00:35:53,618
We should avoid anything
that drives away the true fans

603
00:35:53,684 --> 00:35:55,286
who've backed us for years, right?

604
00:35:58,122 --> 00:35:59,323
Tokushige.

605
00:36:01,259 --> 00:36:05,496
Don't you want
to beat Kohaku in the ratings?

606
00:36:06,097 --> 00:36:07,465
Beat Kohaku?

607
00:36:13,871 --> 00:36:15,106
MR. HATAKEYAMA'S MANAGER-MORITA

608
00:36:15,173 --> 00:36:16,474
Hatakeyama…

609
00:36:17,175 --> 00:36:21,445
You mean the comedian Ippei Hatakeyama?

610
00:36:22,380 --> 00:36:24,682
Now that's impactful casting, right?

611
00:36:24,749 --> 00:36:26,617
I pried open his New Year's schedule.

612
00:36:26,684 --> 00:36:28,152
He even canceled his Hawaii trip.

613
00:36:29,320 --> 00:36:30,688
What do you mean?!

614
00:36:30,755 --> 00:36:33,257
He's popular with every generation,

615
00:36:33,324 --> 00:36:36,961
especially people in their 30s and 40s,
who watch the most TV right now.

616
00:36:37,728 --> 00:36:38,930
I mentioned it to Mr. Tamuken.

617
00:36:38,996 --> 00:36:42,767
When I told him, he loved the idea.
"The Hakone Ekiden? Great!"

618
00:36:43,768 --> 00:36:46,604
You already told President Tamura?!

619
00:36:49,540 --> 00:36:51,342
You can't be serious!

620
00:36:51,409 --> 00:36:53,444
I'm dead serious!

621
00:36:54,345 --> 00:36:57,715
Even you get it, right?
This is Tamuken Pro.

622
00:36:57,782 --> 00:36:59,817
They practically run show business now.

623
00:36:59,884 --> 00:37:01,052
Why would you go and do that?

624
00:37:01,118 --> 00:37:04,455
You didn't move, so I moved for you.

625
00:37:04,522 --> 00:37:05,856
How about a thank you?

626
00:37:08,059 --> 00:37:11,128
Anything like this should go

627
00:37:11,195 --> 00:37:13,297
through my bureau chief first!

628
00:37:14,265 --> 00:37:17,468
You think I went over Kitamura's head?

629
00:37:18,869 --> 00:37:22,006
Mr. Kitamura approved it?

630
00:37:22,073 --> 00:37:23,574
Of course.

631
00:37:28,846 --> 00:37:32,149
Mr. Kuroishi, I'll say it again.

632
00:37:32,783 --> 00:37:35,319
That's not what the Hakone Ekiden is!

633
00:37:35,386 --> 00:37:37,521
Then what is it?

634
00:37:38,656 --> 00:37:40,358
So gathering Ekiden and marathon insiders

635
00:37:40,424 --> 00:37:43,327
to chat among themselves is serious?

636
00:37:43,928 --> 00:37:46,664
If a celebrity joins them,
does that make it frivolous?

637
00:37:46,731 --> 00:37:50,067
That mindset is what makes it boring.
Why don't you notice?

638
00:37:50,134 --> 00:37:53,304
Isn't it a stereotype to think

639
00:37:53,371 --> 00:37:54,839
celebrities guarantee ratings?

640
00:37:58,976 --> 00:38:00,611
You've got some nerve.

641
00:38:02,313 --> 00:38:07,184
The Hakone Ekiden needs
observations grounded in experience

642
00:38:07,251 --> 00:38:10,288
and a deep understanding of the race.

643
00:38:10,354 --> 00:38:13,891
If we let amateurs with no race experience

644
00:38:13,958 --> 00:38:17,762
and questionable passion
for sports comment,

645
00:38:17,828 --> 00:38:19,897
longtime Hakone fans

646
00:38:19,964 --> 00:38:21,966
will be completely turned off!

647
00:38:32,009 --> 00:38:34,912
Tokushige, listen.

648
00:38:36,213 --> 00:38:38,215
Between you and me,

649
00:38:39,917 --> 00:38:42,553
Mr. Kashiwagi agrees with me.

650
00:38:46,490 --> 00:38:48,025
The managing director?

651
00:38:51,095 --> 00:38:52,263
Good morning.

652
00:38:52,330 --> 00:38:54,699
DAINICHI TV MANAGING DIRECTOR
MASAOMI KASHIWAGI

653
00:38:55,933 --> 00:38:57,368
So that's that.

654
00:38:58,769 --> 00:38:59,637
Got it?

655
00:39:13,217 --> 00:39:14,285
HATAKEYAMA'S IT'S SHOWTIME

656
00:39:14,352 --> 00:39:16,153
THURSDAYS AT 8 PM

657
00:39:20,558 --> 00:39:22,193
What's going on, Mr. Kitamura?

658
00:39:22,259 --> 00:39:23,394
About what?

659
00:39:23,461 --> 00:39:26,397
You heard about
Mr. Hatakeyama, didn't you?

660
00:39:26,931 --> 00:39:28,566
Why didn't you tell me right away?

661
00:39:28,632 --> 00:39:31,736
Now that you mention it,
he did say something.

662
00:39:31,802 --> 00:39:34,805
Why didn't you object
when it first came up?

663
00:39:34,872 --> 00:39:35,773
Well,

664
00:39:36,307 --> 00:39:38,209
some trial and error isn't a bad thing.

665
00:39:38,275 --> 00:39:41,178
This is way beyond trial and error!

666
00:39:41,979 --> 00:39:43,681
You know what kind of broadcast

667
00:39:43,748 --> 00:39:46,083
the Hakone Ekiden is!

668
00:39:49,653 --> 00:39:50,788
Managing Director Kashiwagi?

669
00:39:52,156 --> 00:39:55,459
Are you going to bend our principles
for sports broadcasting?

670
00:39:55,526 --> 00:39:56,827
I never said that.

671
00:39:56,894 --> 00:39:58,229
-You basically did.
-When?

672
00:39:58,295 --> 00:39:59,930
It's the same thing.

673
00:40:01,899 --> 00:40:03,367
Listen, Tokushige.

674
00:40:04,101 --> 00:40:08,172
Think about office politics for once.

675
00:40:08,939 --> 00:40:11,208
Mr. Kashiwagi's
probably the next president.

676
00:40:11,275 --> 00:40:13,043
Why go against him?

677
00:40:15,246 --> 00:40:17,648
Are we really putting a comedian
on the Hakone broadcast?

678
00:40:17,715 --> 00:40:19,116
You're okay with that?

679
00:40:19,817 --> 00:40:21,952
Since when did our sports broadcasts

680
00:40:22,019 --> 00:40:23,421
-get so lightweight?
-Shut up, Shige!

681
00:40:23,487 --> 00:40:25,489
I know that without you telling me!

682
00:40:26,157 --> 00:40:28,592
In this company,
when Mr. Kashiwagi says yes,

683
00:40:28,659 --> 00:40:29,960
everyone below has to follow.

684
00:40:30,027 --> 00:40:32,897
-But that doesn't mean--
-I know what you want to say!

685
00:40:34,031 --> 00:40:37,301
So use that stubborn head
of yours and figure it out!

686
00:40:37,368 --> 00:40:39,570
That's your job.

687
00:40:46,977 --> 00:40:49,313
My ears hurt.

688
00:40:51,682 --> 00:40:52,917
You're studying hard.

689
00:40:53,784 --> 00:40:55,686
Natsuki's pressuring me

690
00:40:55,753 --> 00:40:57,655
to watch it all by the end of the week.

691
00:40:57,721 --> 00:40:59,623
Isn't this workplace bullying?

692
00:41:00,491 --> 00:41:02,092
Hey, Tokushige!

693
00:41:02,660 --> 00:41:05,329
I said give me a wide shot of Tozai! Wide!

694
00:41:05,396 --> 00:41:06,530
That year,

695
00:41:06,597 --> 00:41:08,265
the weathervane was a broadcast director.

696
00:41:08,332 --> 00:41:10,000
I was the director in Car One.

697
00:41:10,067 --> 00:41:13,137
I'm talking to you, Shige! Answer me!

698
00:41:13,204 --> 00:41:16,006
That's scary! He's totally losing it!

699
00:41:16,640 --> 00:41:19,710
-I said look!
-He was really scary back then.

700
00:41:20,277 --> 00:41:22,246
TEN YEARS AGO

701
00:41:22,313 --> 00:41:26,083
Shige, I told you to get
his feet in the shot!

702
00:41:26,150 --> 00:41:27,751
I want his expression. Stay tight.

703
00:41:28,352 --> 00:41:30,588
-Please show a close-up.
-Idiot!

704
00:41:30,654 --> 00:41:32,590
I said show his whole body!

705
00:41:32,656 --> 00:41:34,792
Hold it right there!

706
00:41:35,359 --> 00:41:37,728
You're the next broadcast director.

707
00:41:38,496 --> 00:41:39,763
I recommended you.

708
00:41:40,364 --> 00:41:41,499
Seriously?

709
00:41:42,233 --> 00:41:44,602
When you zoomed in on that runner's face,

710
00:41:45,603 --> 00:41:47,438
that worked too.

711
00:41:50,708 --> 00:41:51,709
I'm counting on you.

712
00:41:53,677 --> 00:41:54,745
Yes!

713
00:41:55,546 --> 00:41:57,314
-Ow!
-Give it your best.

714
00:41:57,381 --> 00:41:58,949
-Give it your best.
-That hurts!

715
00:41:59,783 --> 00:42:04,855
He probably didn't want
to give up being broadcast director.

716
00:42:20,804 --> 00:42:23,807
THE HAKONE EKIDEN BROADCAST HANDBOOK
NUMBERS 1-17

717
00:42:27,444 --> 00:42:28,512
NUMBERS 23-39

718
00:42:52,469 --> 00:42:56,106
It's a pleasure to meet you.
I'm Tokushige from Dainichi TV.

719
00:42:56,173 --> 00:42:57,341
Sit.

720
00:42:58,475 --> 00:43:01,645
-Thank you.
-Hello, I'm Tamura.

721
00:43:01,712 --> 00:43:03,614
I may not look it, but I'm busy.

722
00:43:03,681 --> 00:43:05,316
So nothing boring, okay?

723
00:43:07,985 --> 00:43:10,354
Please take good care of our Hatakeyama.

724
00:43:10,421 --> 00:43:11,989
He's all fired up.

725
00:43:12,523 --> 00:43:14,024
I think it'll make a great show.

726
00:43:15,826 --> 00:43:17,394
Honestly,

727
00:43:18,062 --> 00:43:21,565
I've hardly ever watched it. But my wife's

728
00:43:21,632 --> 00:43:23,901
a huge Hakone Ekiden fan.

729
00:43:23,968 --> 00:43:27,605
You know that hill past Yokohama?
What's it called?

730
00:43:28,405 --> 00:43:30,207
Gontazaka?
The toughest part of the second leg.

731
00:43:30,274 --> 00:43:31,842
That's the one!

732
00:43:31,909 --> 00:43:35,346
She made me buy a condo
with a view of that hill.

733
00:43:35,412 --> 00:43:36,880
Just to watch the Ekiden!

734
00:43:37,681 --> 00:43:38,682
Jeez…

735
00:43:38,749 --> 00:43:41,485
At New Year's, she watches TV,

736
00:43:41,552 --> 00:43:45,055
then the hill, then TV, then the hill.

737
00:43:45,956 --> 00:43:47,458
She totally ignores me.

738
00:43:47,524 --> 00:43:53,030
So personally, I'm a little jealous
of the Hakone Ekiden.

739
00:43:54,031 --> 00:43:57,334
Oh, and on clear days,

740
00:43:57,401 --> 00:43:59,803
you can see Dainichi TV in the distance.

741
00:44:00,337 --> 00:44:03,540
I might be spying on you
with binoculars, so watch out.

742
00:44:09,780 --> 00:44:10,881
Thank you.

743
00:44:17,855 --> 00:44:20,257
Um, President Tamura.

744
00:44:21,158 --> 00:44:22,960
There's something I'd like you to hear.

745
00:44:24,128 --> 00:44:24,962
What?

746
00:44:26,130 --> 00:44:28,032
I'd like to tell you about 1987,

747
00:44:28,732 --> 00:44:33,037
when we first aired Hakone live.

748
00:44:34,605 --> 00:44:38,542
Back then, everyone said
a live broadcast was impossible.

749
00:44:39,443 --> 00:44:43,781
The Hakone Mountains
blocked the radio waves.

750
00:44:43,847 --> 00:44:45,315
They simply couldn't get through.

751
00:44:47,184 --> 00:44:52,156
After much thought, the staff decided
to put relay equipment

752
00:44:52,690 --> 00:44:54,758
on the summit.

753
00:44:56,527 --> 00:44:58,328
Hauling dozens of kilos

754
00:44:58,395 --> 00:45:01,665
of equipment up trackless slopes

755
00:45:02,332 --> 00:45:04,101
was a matter of life and death.

756
00:45:05,202 --> 00:45:08,839
Why were they so set on a live broadcast?

757
00:45:10,007 --> 00:45:13,310
Because they wanted

758
00:45:14,178 --> 00:45:16,146
to capture the runners in the moment.

759
00:45:17,915 --> 00:45:21,552
The Hakone Ekiden is a race
where the runners are the stars.

760
00:45:22,753 --> 00:45:28,325
Our job is to show the students
as they are, in the moment,

761
00:45:29,426 --> 00:45:33,263
and to convey every nuance
of the race thoroughly and accurately.

762
00:45:34,031 --> 00:45:39,970
So the staff and commentators
stay in supporting roles.

763
00:45:40,971 --> 00:45:45,843
We simply show the runners
and their race as it happens.

764
00:45:46,877 --> 00:45:51,315
That's why we've never invited

765
00:45:52,182 --> 00:45:54,151
a celebrity as a guest.

766
00:45:55,185 --> 00:45:56,920
"The more times change,

767
00:45:58,255 --> 00:46:01,525
the more valuable
the unchanging Hakone Ekiden becomes."

768
00:46:02,459 --> 00:46:05,729
Those were the words
of our first producer.

769
00:46:06,764 --> 00:46:10,634
With that resolve to never change,

770
00:46:11,401 --> 00:46:15,005
we've protected the broadcast every year.

771
00:46:17,174 --> 00:46:21,578
I don't know
what you and Kuroishi discussed,

772
00:46:23,180 --> 00:46:27,618
but for now, we don't plan

773
00:46:28,852 --> 00:46:32,523
to have Mr. Hatakeyama
on the Hakone Ekiden.

774
00:46:36,093 --> 00:46:38,862
I'm truly sorry.

775
00:46:44,668 --> 00:46:47,771
So you don't need Hatakeyama?

776
00:46:51,708 --> 00:46:53,577
Is Kuroishi saying that too?

777
00:46:54,511 --> 00:46:57,714
Kuroishi is the Programming Bureau Chief,

778
00:46:59,316 --> 00:47:03,620
but I'm fully responsible
for producing Hakone.

779
00:47:03,687 --> 00:47:04,822
That's not what I'm asking!

780
00:47:07,558 --> 00:47:10,394
If you don't need our celebrities, fine.

781
00:47:11,628 --> 00:47:13,230
From now on,

782
00:47:13,297 --> 00:47:16,633
all Tamuken Pro
celebrities will stay off Dainichi TV.

783
00:47:17,935 --> 00:47:19,269
Not just sports.

784
00:47:19,336 --> 00:47:22,739
Variety shows and dramas too.

785
00:47:23,874 --> 00:47:25,142
Sir, please wait…

786
00:47:25,209 --> 00:47:28,579
-Take the rest up with Kuroishi.
-Sir!

787
00:47:36,320 --> 00:47:38,822
You damn idiot! Mr. Tamuken is furious!

788
00:47:39,423 --> 00:47:41,558
Go apologize now.
Get on your knees if you have to!

789
00:47:43,861 --> 00:47:45,195
I'm sorry,

790
00:47:46,029 --> 00:47:50,801
but please let us broadcast
the Hakone Ekiden as usual.

791
00:47:50,868 --> 00:47:54,004
You're going against
Managing Director Kashiwagi's wishes?

792
00:47:55,105 --> 00:47:56,974
I'd follow him if he were right.

793
00:47:58,075 --> 00:47:59,476
But he's not.

794
00:48:00,544 --> 00:48:01,778
Listen.

795
00:48:01,845 --> 00:48:05,249
The Hakone Ekiden doesn't belong to you!

796
00:48:06,183 --> 00:48:08,185
It doesn't belong to
the Sports Department either.

797
00:48:08,919 --> 00:48:12,556
It's Dainichi TV's precious asset!

798
00:48:13,924 --> 00:48:15,626
Don't forget that.

799
00:48:19,730 --> 00:48:20,631
Mr. Kuroishi.

800
00:48:21,164 --> 00:48:22,266
What?

801
00:48:23,834 --> 00:48:30,240
The Hakone Ekiden doesn't belong
to me or to Sports Department.

802
00:48:31,441 --> 00:48:32,342
And…

803
00:48:34,144 --> 00:48:36,113
it doesn't belong to Dainichi TV.

804
00:48:41,084 --> 00:48:42,719
It belongs to the runners.

805
00:48:47,090 --> 00:48:49,359
You've got some nerve.

806
00:48:51,495 --> 00:48:53,063
Listen carefully, Tokushige.

807
00:48:54,831 --> 00:48:57,034
You've got two choices.

808
00:48:58,568 --> 00:49:02,906
Get on your knees to Mr. Tamuken
and have Hatakeyama on Hakone,

809
00:49:03,607 --> 00:49:06,276
or take the blame for losing

810
00:49:06,343 --> 00:49:10,047
all Tamuken Pro celebrities
from Dainichi TV.

811
00:49:10,113 --> 00:49:12,716
I want your decision

812
00:49:12,783 --> 00:49:15,452
by the executive meeting early next week.

813
00:49:18,755 --> 00:49:22,793
MEISEI GAKUIN UNIVERSITY
TRACK AND FIELD TEAM

814
00:49:51,388 --> 00:49:54,591
From now on,
we'll meet as a group twice a month.

815
00:49:54,658 --> 00:49:58,628
You'll set goals at the start
of the month and check your progress.

816
00:49:58,695 --> 00:50:01,498
Then think about what you need to do

817
00:50:01,565 --> 00:50:02,866
to reach them.

818
00:50:03,867 --> 00:50:06,003
Each of you, set goals for your running

819
00:50:06,069 --> 00:50:09,373
that are as specific as possible.

820
00:50:10,173 --> 00:50:12,642
That's it for practice today.

821
00:50:12,709 --> 00:50:14,611
-Good work.
-Um…

822
00:50:17,581 --> 00:50:19,516
You told each of us to set

823
00:50:19,583 --> 00:50:21,251
specific goals.

824
00:50:22,486 --> 00:50:23,587
But before that,

825
00:50:24,521 --> 00:50:27,290
could you tell us
your coaching philosophy?

826
00:50:29,092 --> 00:50:32,396
What I just said
is my coaching philosophy.

827
00:50:41,204 --> 00:50:43,006
-Mr. Nomura, did you hear?
-Huh?

828
00:50:43,073 --> 00:50:45,876
A Tamuken Pro actor
might suddenly drop out,

829
00:50:45,942 --> 00:50:48,645
so the January drama can't start shooting.

830
00:50:50,180 --> 00:50:51,448
Oh, really?

831
00:50:51,515 --> 00:50:54,284
Next week's Hatakeyama's It's Showtime

832
00:50:54,351 --> 00:50:55,652
taping got postponed too.

833
00:50:55,719 --> 00:50:58,088
What? I was scheduled to shoot that.

834
00:50:58,155 --> 00:51:00,190
My location shoot today got canceled

835
00:51:00,257 --> 00:51:02,025
because the Tamuken celebrity can't come.

836
00:51:02,092 --> 00:51:03,994
It was my first variety gig in ages.

837
00:51:04,861 --> 00:51:07,531
Mr. Tokushige really did it this time.

838
00:51:09,733 --> 00:51:12,436
Mr. Yasuhara, whose side are you on?

839
00:51:12,502 --> 00:51:15,939
Huh? It's not about sides.

840
00:51:16,006 --> 00:51:19,342
Is this Mr. Tokushige's fault?

841
00:51:22,279 --> 00:51:23,747
Right.

842
00:51:23,814 --> 00:51:26,316
The real problem is Kuroishi

843
00:51:26,383 --> 00:51:28,785
pushing ahead and ignoring the crew.

844
00:51:28,852 --> 00:51:30,554
Totally. I bet he just sees Hakone

845
00:51:30,620 --> 00:51:33,190
as popular content.

846
00:51:33,256 --> 00:51:35,859
I want Mr. Tokushige
to really fight back too.

847
00:51:37,360 --> 00:51:40,197
-Good morning.
-Good morning.

848
00:51:58,014 --> 00:51:58,882
What's up?

849
00:52:00,517 --> 00:52:03,720
Well, I guess I know what's up.

850
00:52:05,755 --> 00:52:06,723
Is it okay?

851
00:52:07,524 --> 00:52:08,358
‎Yeah.

852
00:52:08,892 --> 00:52:13,096
I've been on an apology tour
around the building all morning.

853
00:52:15,465 --> 00:52:16,566
But it's okay.

854
00:52:17,434 --> 00:52:19,035
I'll figure something out.

855
00:52:20,137 --> 00:52:23,140
Don't worry. Just keep working.

856
00:52:23,807 --> 00:52:25,775
-Okay.
-Okay.

857
00:52:27,444 --> 00:52:30,881
Though I guess you can't help worrying.

858
00:52:36,653 --> 00:52:37,721
Hold on!

859
00:52:40,624 --> 00:52:42,559
What do you mean, "frivolous"?!

860
00:52:44,361 --> 00:52:47,197
How are we frivolous?!

861
00:52:48,865 --> 00:52:50,400
Say something!

862
00:52:54,070 --> 00:52:56,473
We've got trouble! There's a fight!

863
00:52:56,540 --> 00:52:58,508
-Who?
-Natsuki.

864
00:52:58,575 --> 00:52:59,609
Ms. Miyamoto?

865
00:52:59,676 --> 00:53:02,179
She's arguing downstairs
with a variety director from her year.

866
00:53:02,245 --> 00:53:03,580
Variety?

867
00:53:03,647 --> 00:53:05,582
A Tamuken Pro
pop idol might quit their show.

868
00:53:05,649 --> 00:53:07,851
They were glaring at each other.

869
00:53:07,918 --> 00:53:09,452
It was all "Take responsibility!"

870
00:53:21,131 --> 00:53:22,966
Um, Mr. Tokushige.

871
00:53:25,869 --> 00:53:30,574
Maybe we could reconsider
having Mr. Hatakeyama on after all.

872
00:53:32,075 --> 00:53:35,245
Of course, we'd get creative
with how he appears,

873
00:53:35,879 --> 00:53:39,316
as long as we protect the way
Hakone's always been broadcast.

874
00:53:44,654 --> 00:53:45,555
Um…

875
00:53:46,856 --> 00:53:49,426
-I think so too.
-Toyama.

876
00:53:50,460 --> 00:53:51,962
I mean, why not, right?

877
00:53:52,028 --> 00:53:54,264
People who want to see Mr. Hatakeyama

878
00:53:54,331 --> 00:53:56,433
might come to love Hakone because of this.

879
00:53:57,334 --> 00:53:59,469
Giving viewers what they want to see

880
00:53:59,536 --> 00:54:01,504
is part of our job too.

881
00:54:02,906 --> 00:54:03,940
Is it?

882
00:54:06,810 --> 00:54:08,478
"Giving them what they want to see"

883
00:54:09,012 --> 00:54:12,716
just sounds like pandering to me.

884
00:54:13,783 --> 00:54:15,719
Isn't giving viewers something

885
00:54:15,785 --> 00:54:19,055
that moves them for a lifetime

886
00:54:20,190 --> 00:54:22,259
worth far more than a fleeting number?

887
00:54:26,363 --> 00:54:27,998
I'm against

888
00:54:28,064 --> 00:54:31,167
bringing frivolous variety stuff

889
00:54:32,302 --> 00:54:33,870
into sports broadcasting.

890
00:54:38,308 --> 00:54:39,342
Miyamoto.

891
00:54:40,577 --> 00:54:43,580
Have you ever
really watched a variety show?

892
00:54:45,482 --> 00:54:46,449
You know,

893
00:54:46,516 --> 00:54:51,521
before I came here,
I was a variety director for eight years.

894
00:54:52,222 --> 00:54:53,923
That's not the only reason I say this.

895
00:54:54,658 --> 00:54:58,528
But just as you approach
sports with conviction,

896
00:54:59,095 --> 00:55:03,233
I know those guys pour their souls
into making variety.

897
00:55:04,668 --> 00:55:08,905
Getting ratings is part of our job
as TV people too.

898
00:55:09,973 --> 00:55:14,411
That's true for sports and variety alike.

899
00:55:15,512 --> 00:55:17,447
Nobody has the right

900
00:55:18,481 --> 00:55:21,318
to mock someone else's serious work.

901
00:55:29,159 --> 00:55:30,260
What's the show called?

902
00:55:32,329 --> 00:55:34,331
The one the Tamuken Pro pop idol quit.

903
00:55:35,532 --> 00:55:37,767
It's a late-night show
called Laugh to Death.

904
00:55:43,206 --> 00:55:44,941
LAUGH TO DEATH

905
00:55:45,742 --> 00:55:47,911
Are you really okay with this,
Mr. Watanabe?

906
00:55:47,977 --> 00:55:50,380
Hey, what about
the foot-pressure rehearsal?

907
00:55:50,447 --> 00:55:51,514
Yes.

908
00:55:59,456 --> 00:56:01,291
Hey.

909
00:56:01,358 --> 00:56:02,459
Oh. Mr. Tokushige!

910
00:56:03,259 --> 00:56:05,095
-Long time no see.
-Yeah.

911
00:56:06,463 --> 00:56:07,297
Well…

912
00:56:08,465 --> 00:56:09,432
I'm so sorry.

913
00:56:11,301 --> 00:56:13,370
I heard your cast member quit.

914
00:56:13,870 --> 00:56:17,540
I caused trouble for the show you started.

915
00:56:18,675 --> 00:56:19,976
I'm really sorry.

916
00:56:22,145 --> 00:56:25,749
If you like, I can find athletes

917
00:56:25,815 --> 00:56:27,650
who understand variety shows

918
00:56:27,717 --> 00:56:29,652
-for guest spots…
-It's fine, Mr. Tokushige.

919
00:56:30,720 --> 00:56:32,789
-No, but…
-Really, it's fine.

920
00:56:34,023 --> 00:56:35,892
If anything, I'm grateful.

921
00:56:36,926 --> 00:56:38,962
-Huh?
-Actually,

922
00:56:39,028 --> 00:56:41,131
the Tamuken Pro pop idol who wanted out

923
00:56:41,698 --> 00:56:44,934
was brought in by Programming
to boost the show.

924
00:56:47,537 --> 00:56:51,441
We launched Laugh to Death

925
00:56:51,508 --> 00:56:53,009
around comedians going all out.

926
00:56:53,076 --> 00:56:53,910
BRAINSTORMING MEETING

927
00:56:53,977 --> 00:56:56,846
So we're getting back to our roots.

928
00:56:57,647 --> 00:56:59,315
More importantly, Mr. Tokushige.

929
00:57:00,450 --> 00:57:04,387
I heard Bureau Chief Kuroishi
is trying to change Hakone.

930
00:57:07,357 --> 00:57:10,693
Don't give an inch.

931
00:57:34,017 --> 00:57:36,419
-Ready, start!
-Okay!

932
00:57:38,955 --> 00:57:40,156
Pick up the speed a little!

933
00:57:40,223 --> 00:57:43,426
No! This really hurts!

934
00:57:43,493 --> 00:57:44,961
You got this! Two more meters!

935
00:57:46,262 --> 00:57:48,498
Lowering your foot more
will make it look more real!

936
00:57:48,565 --> 00:57:49,532
Keep it gritty.

937
00:57:50,099 --> 00:57:52,769
-Get the sweat. Sweat!
-Sweat!

938
00:57:52,836 --> 00:57:53,903
A little tighter!

939
00:57:53,970 --> 00:57:56,473
-Yes!
-A little more!

940
00:57:56,539 --> 00:57:59,843
LAUGH TO DEATH

941
00:58:01,544 --> 00:58:02,445
Um…

942
00:58:04,147 --> 00:58:04,981
Yes?

943
00:58:05,648 --> 00:58:07,684
I'm Miyamoto from the Sports Department.

944
00:58:07,750 --> 00:58:11,688
Miyamoto… From the Hakone Ekiden?

945
00:58:12,489 --> 00:58:13,723
Yes.

946
00:58:15,458 --> 00:58:16,493
What can I do for you?

947
00:58:18,294 --> 00:58:19,896
I came to ask you a favor.

948
00:58:24,934 --> 00:58:26,903
REGARDING TAMUKEN PRO

949
00:58:26,970 --> 00:58:27,904
RYO TOKUSHIGE

950
00:58:27,971 --> 00:58:29,038
WE APOLOGIZE

951
00:58:29,105 --> 00:58:30,006
FOR THE CASTING ISSUE.

952
00:58:47,924 --> 00:58:51,127
THE HAKONE EKIDEN BROADCAST HANDBOOK

953
00:58:52,662 --> 00:58:53,696
63RD EKIDEN

954
00:58:53,763 --> 00:58:54,864
EKIDEN BROADCAST HANDBOOK

955
00:59:12,282 --> 00:59:13,583
Mr. Tokushige, what are you doing?

956
00:59:16,386 --> 00:59:19,489
You know the saying.
"When in trouble, turn to the handbook."

957
00:59:19,556 --> 00:59:20,590
BROADCAST HANDBOOK-MANUAL

958
00:59:20,657 --> 00:59:27,063
SHOWING RUNNER'S INFORMATION
AND CAMERA POSITION

959
00:59:29,098 --> 00:59:30,533
Did you find the answer?

960
00:59:30,600 --> 00:59:35,438
It's not that easy.

961
00:59:38,641 --> 00:59:41,611
Seeing them all like this,
there are so many.

962
00:59:43,012 --> 00:59:44,981
It's history. Truly.

963
00:59:49,986 --> 00:59:50,954
Oh, sorry.

964
00:59:51,955 --> 00:59:53,723
This is hilarious.

965
00:59:54,324 --> 00:59:56,926
Next, we wrap up briefly at center,
then go back to Car Three.

966
00:59:56,993 --> 00:59:58,561
Hold the commercial!

967
00:59:58,628 --> 01:00:00,496
Mr. Tokushige, we should go to commercial.

968
01:00:00,563 --> 01:00:01,931
Is it that?

969
01:00:01,998 --> 01:00:04,367
That's from when
Miyamoto directed Car Three.

970
01:00:04,434 --> 01:00:07,236
You two had this gap even back then.

971
01:00:07,303 --> 01:00:08,805
I think we should go now.

972
01:00:08,871 --> 01:00:10,373
I said we're waiting!

973
01:00:10,440 --> 01:00:12,976
Nishiwaki of Teikyo University
has gradually improved his pace

974
01:00:13,042 --> 01:00:14,911
since the five-kilometer mark.

975
01:00:14,978 --> 01:00:17,747
But even if he passes the school ahead,
it'll take about three minutes.

976
01:00:17,814 --> 01:00:19,749
We should go to commercial now.

977
01:00:19,816 --> 01:00:20,984
Go to commercial!

978
01:00:21,050 --> 01:00:22,685
Come on!

979
01:00:22,752 --> 01:00:24,821
Doesn't the broadcast director
have any pride?

980
01:00:24,887 --> 01:00:28,291
No, it's not about pride.
Commercials matter.

981
01:00:33,896 --> 01:00:34,764
Is everything okay…

982
01:00:34,831 --> 01:00:35,665
MANAGING DIR. OFFICE

983
01:00:35,732 --> 01:00:37,000
…with the Tamuken Pro issue?

984
01:00:37,600 --> 01:00:40,370
I'm pulling together
where things stand across the company.

985
01:00:43,172 --> 01:00:45,775
What do you plan to do now?

986
01:00:48,044 --> 01:00:50,413
Tokushige will take full responsibility.

987
01:00:51,214 --> 01:00:52,281
Responsibility?

988
01:00:54,684 --> 01:00:59,489
I'll take him off Hakone.

989
01:01:00,990 --> 01:01:03,426
Hello, thank you as always.

990
01:01:03,493 --> 01:01:05,862
This is Tokushige from Dainichi TV.

991
01:01:06,996 --> 01:01:07,897
MEISEI GAKUIN UNIVERSITY

992
01:01:07,964 --> 01:01:08,898
TRACK AND FIELD DORMITORY

993
01:01:10,133 --> 01:01:11,200
Excuse me.

994
01:01:12,035 --> 01:01:12,869
What is it?

995
01:01:13,736 --> 01:01:17,073
Coach, could I talk to you
about something?

996
01:01:24,180 --> 01:01:26,716
I heard about it.

997
01:01:27,850 --> 01:01:30,620
Tohto Chuo Bussan's community program.

998
01:01:31,654 --> 01:01:35,692
And that you'll only coach for one year.

999
01:01:41,631 --> 01:01:42,598
But…

1000
01:01:43,566 --> 01:01:46,536
can you build a team
that makes it to Hakone that way?

1001
01:01:48,371 --> 01:01:50,707
A lot of the team isn't convinced.

1002
01:01:55,545 --> 01:01:56,446
And you?

1003
01:01:57,547 --> 01:01:59,682
-Huh?
-What do you think?

1004
01:02:03,953 --> 01:02:07,457
I think one year will be tough.

1005
01:02:09,992 --> 01:02:11,427
But right now,

1006
01:02:12,228 --> 01:02:15,531
I think the problem
is that the team is divided.

1007
01:02:18,367 --> 01:02:21,037
I know that as captain,

1008
01:02:21,704 --> 01:02:26,008
I should be the one
to pull us together, but…

1009
01:02:28,478 --> 01:02:31,347
"I cost us the qualifying race.

1010
01:02:31,414 --> 01:02:32,648
I don't have the confidence."

1011
01:02:34,851 --> 01:02:35,952
Is that it?

1012
01:02:42,492 --> 01:02:43,626
Yes.

1013
01:02:44,794 --> 01:02:45,995
It's because of me…

1014
01:02:48,331 --> 01:02:50,466
that our team didn't make Hakone.

1015
01:02:51,968 --> 01:02:55,738
And that's why you're unsure
about running for the Student United Team.

1016
01:03:05,248 --> 01:03:06,215
Do I even

1017
01:03:08,117 --> 01:03:10,286
deserve to run Hakone?

1018
01:03:13,422 --> 01:03:18,294
Isn't resolve more important than
whether you deserve it?

1019
01:03:19,328 --> 01:03:20,229
Huh?

1020
01:03:20,296 --> 01:03:22,265
If you turn it down,

1021
01:03:22,832 --> 01:03:25,601
what happens
to the guys criticizing you now?

1022
01:03:29,172 --> 01:03:30,406
They'd be hurt, don't you think?

1023
01:03:32,041 --> 01:03:32,875
Hurt?

1024
01:03:32,942 --> 01:03:34,610
"He gave up

1025
01:03:35,478 --> 01:03:37,146
Hakone because of me."

1026
01:03:38,614 --> 01:03:40,449
Do you want them to regret that?

1027
01:03:43,186 --> 01:03:47,356
Anger is much easier than regret.

1028
01:03:50,927 --> 01:03:55,631
Next week, I'll gather the runners
picked for the Student United Team

1029
01:03:56,232 --> 01:03:57,700
and begin team practice.

1030
01:04:04,841 --> 01:04:08,778
I'm staking my future

1031
01:04:08,845 --> 01:04:10,713
as a coach on this Hakone.

1032
01:04:12,248 --> 01:04:15,451
Aoba, make the team

1033
01:04:16,919 --> 01:04:18,688
accept you with your running.

1034
01:04:20,456 --> 01:04:23,392
Until then, don't listen
to any of the noise.

1035
01:04:24,727 --> 01:04:26,329
I'll hear the complaints after Hakone.

1036
01:04:28,931 --> 01:04:29,899
How about it, Aoba?

1037
01:04:31,267 --> 01:04:32,134
Can you do it?

1038
01:04:36,539 --> 01:04:37,573
I can.

1039
01:04:39,175 --> 01:04:43,880
DAY OF EXECUTIVE MEETING

1040
01:04:49,452 --> 01:04:50,286
Yes.

1041
01:04:51,888 --> 01:04:52,822
Thank you for waiting.

1042
01:04:55,491 --> 01:04:56,525
Okay.

1043
01:05:01,063 --> 01:05:02,131
Will he be okay?

1044
01:05:02,198 --> 01:05:04,567
The executive meeting is soon, right?

1045
01:05:05,968 --> 01:05:08,004
He'll be fine. It's Mr. Tokushige.

1046
01:05:18,781 --> 01:05:19,649
Right this way.

1047
01:05:19,715 --> 01:05:20,549
EXECUTIVE ROOM

1048
01:05:26,589 --> 01:05:27,456
Please.

1049
01:05:38,434 --> 01:05:39,435
Have a seat.

1050
01:05:58,888 --> 01:06:00,256
DAINICHI TV PRESIDENT
HIDEHIKO TAKESHIBA

1051
01:06:00,323 --> 01:06:02,792
Let's move to the last item on the agenda.

1052
01:06:02,858 --> 01:06:06,429
Our chief producer for the Hakone Ekiden,
Tokushige,

1053
01:06:06,495 --> 01:06:09,365
will explain what happened.

1054
01:06:09,432 --> 01:06:12,001
Losing Tamuken Pro's trust is a major blow

1055
01:06:12,568 --> 01:06:15,871
to our drama and variety divisions.

1056
01:06:16,639 --> 01:06:19,775
It's already disrupted production
of several programs.

1057
01:06:22,111 --> 01:06:23,346
Tokushige,

1058
01:06:24,280 --> 01:06:26,015
please explain how this came about.

1059
01:06:27,650 --> 01:06:28,651
Yes.

1060
01:06:33,956 --> 01:06:35,424
Before I do,

1061
01:06:35,992 --> 01:06:39,295
may I share something with everyone?

1062
01:06:39,362 --> 01:06:40,429
Is it okay?

1063
01:06:48,437 --> 01:06:52,675
This is what we call

1064
01:06:52,742 --> 01:06:54,276
the Hakone Ekiden Broadcast Handbook.

1065
01:06:54,877 --> 01:06:57,380
It contains everything,

1066
01:06:57,446 --> 01:07:00,082
from runner info to camera positions.

1067
01:07:00,149 --> 01:07:04,420
It's essentially a manual
for broadcasting the Hakone Ekiden.

1068
01:07:04,487 --> 01:07:07,123
But that's not all.

1069
01:07:08,557 --> 01:07:10,459
It records our passion

1070
01:07:10,526 --> 01:07:11,994
for each year's broadcast.

1071
01:07:12,061 --> 01:07:16,399
It's an emotional anchor for us.

1072
01:07:16,465 --> 01:07:19,802
What does that have to do
with today's agenda?

1073
01:07:22,104 --> 01:07:25,207
This is the very first

1074
01:07:25,741 --> 01:07:28,377
broadcast handbook.

1075
01:07:29,678 --> 01:07:30,880
Please look here.

1076
01:07:31,614 --> 01:07:33,516
63RD

1077
01:07:33,582 --> 01:07:35,618
It says "63rd."

1078
01:07:35,684 --> 01:07:36,952
Yes.

1079
01:07:37,653 --> 01:07:39,422
Why does our first broadcast

1080
01:07:39,955 --> 01:07:42,058
say 63rd?

1081
01:07:42,992 --> 01:07:46,762
Because we only started

1082
01:07:47,296 --> 01:07:50,332
broadcasting from the 63rd race.

1083
01:07:50,399 --> 01:07:51,300
I asked

1084
01:07:52,535 --> 01:07:55,905
what this has to do with today's meeting!

1085
01:07:57,773 --> 01:08:00,176
The first race

1086
01:08:00,242 --> 01:08:02,511
was held in 1920.

1087
01:08:03,179 --> 01:08:07,183
It's gone on for over a century.

1088
01:08:08,217 --> 01:08:11,387
Over its long history,

1089
01:08:11,454 --> 01:08:14,957
the Hakone Ekiden was halted by war.

1090
01:08:16,292 --> 01:08:17,393
But even then,

1091
01:08:18,327 --> 01:08:20,463
the runners wanted to run

1092
01:08:21,030 --> 01:08:22,798
through the ruins of Tokyo again.

1093
01:08:23,432 --> 01:08:25,000
They wanted to pass the sash.

1094
01:08:26,202 --> 01:08:27,803
They never gave up running.

1095
01:08:29,672 --> 01:08:33,542
The Hakone Ekiden was started by runners

1096
01:08:33,609 --> 01:08:36,645
and kept alive by runners.

1097
01:08:37,746 --> 01:08:39,915
Our job as a TV station

1098
01:08:39,982 --> 01:08:42,618
is to show their race as it truly is.

1099
01:08:42,685 --> 01:08:46,255
Exactly as it happens.

1100
01:08:47,056 --> 01:08:48,491
Nothing more.

1101
01:08:56,866 --> 01:08:57,766
Hey.

1102
01:08:58,868 --> 01:09:00,136
Enough already.

1103
01:09:01,070 --> 01:09:02,972
That's not what I'm asking.

1104
01:09:03,539 --> 01:09:05,674
Your reckless actions
have already disrupted

1105
01:09:05,741 --> 01:09:07,543
our programming.

1106
01:09:07,610 --> 01:09:09,778
How will you take responsibility?

1107
01:09:09,845 --> 01:09:11,147
That's what I'm asking!

1108
01:09:11,213 --> 01:09:13,149
Do you understand

1109
01:09:13,215 --> 01:09:14,650
how serious your mistake is?

1110
01:09:17,953 --> 01:09:20,322
I'm the chief producer
of the Hakone Ekiden.

1111
01:09:20,389 --> 01:09:21,323
So what?

1112
01:09:22,057 --> 01:09:22,892
As you say,

1113
01:09:23,626 --> 01:09:25,561
all responsibility lies with me.

1114
01:09:26,428 --> 01:09:27,696
But that also means

1115
01:09:27,763 --> 01:09:31,033
the authority to decide the broadcast

1116
01:09:31,100 --> 01:09:32,401
should be mine.

1117
01:09:34,203 --> 01:09:37,973
Sir, he's trying to change the subject.

1118
01:09:38,040 --> 01:09:39,341
The problem is…

1119
01:09:40,576 --> 01:09:42,411
his reckless actions

1120
01:09:42,945 --> 01:09:46,248
have caused major losses.

1121
01:09:47,816 --> 01:09:49,051
Bureau Chief Kuroishi.

1122
01:09:49,718 --> 01:09:52,855
This isn't just me acting on my own.

1123
01:09:53,889 --> 01:09:54,890
What do you mean?

1124
01:09:56,892 --> 01:10:02,798
Actually, our sponsor, Miyako Beer
made a request the other day.

1125
01:10:03,465 --> 01:10:04,767
Miyako Beer did?

1126
01:10:04,833 --> 01:10:06,368
Miyako Beer did?

1127
01:10:06,936 --> 01:10:08,404
What is it?

1128
01:10:08,470 --> 01:10:11,907
They can't support a format

1129
01:10:11,974 --> 01:10:15,611
that casts celebrities.

1130
01:10:17,546 --> 01:10:20,516
-Miyako Beer said that?
-Really?

1131
01:10:20,583 --> 01:10:22,117
What a bluff.

1132
01:10:23,452 --> 01:10:24,620
It's not a bluff.

1133
01:10:25,621 --> 01:10:26,755
Fine.

1134
01:10:26,822 --> 01:10:28,424
I'll check with Miyako Beer myself.

1135
01:10:28,991 --> 01:10:31,660
There's no need.

1136
01:10:37,399 --> 01:10:39,768
Sorry to keep you waiting.
I'll put you through now.

1137
01:10:41,237 --> 01:10:42,805
-Excuse me.
-Yes.

1138
01:10:44,073 --> 01:10:47,109
Could you put this on that monitor?

1139
01:10:47,676 --> 01:10:49,278
I'm connected with Miyako Beer.

1140
01:10:49,345 --> 01:10:50,179
Huh?

1141
01:11:00,189 --> 01:11:01,023
Put it through.

1142
01:11:02,091 --> 01:11:03,058
Thank you.

1143
01:11:07,963 --> 01:11:09,064
It's connected.

1144
01:11:12,935 --> 01:11:15,638
This is Mr. Sone,
sales director at Miyako Beer.

1145
01:11:17,673 --> 01:11:20,109
Mr. Sone, please take it from here.

1146
01:11:20,809 --> 01:11:23,012
My apologies for interrupting

1147
01:11:23,078 --> 01:11:25,814
your important executive meeting.

1148
01:11:27,016 --> 01:11:30,352
I asked for your valuable time today

1149
01:11:30,419 --> 01:11:34,023
to restate our basic sponsorship policy.

1150
01:11:34,590 --> 01:11:37,092
At Miyako Beer,

1151
01:11:37,693 --> 01:11:38,761
we want the Hakone Ekiden

1152
01:11:40,195 --> 01:11:43,299
broadcast in its usual format.

1153
01:11:44,633 --> 01:11:46,402
Unfortunately,

1154
01:11:46,468 --> 01:11:49,171
we can't agree to changes
such as bringing in

1155
01:11:49,238 --> 01:11:51,707
celebrities as guests or hosts.

1156
01:11:53,876 --> 01:11:55,144
Hello.

1157
01:11:55,678 --> 01:11:57,446
I'm Managing Director Kashiwagi.

1158
01:11:58,013 --> 01:11:58,914
Mr. Sone.

1159
01:11:59,948 --> 01:12:02,951
Is that your company's official position?

1160
01:12:04,153 --> 01:12:05,154
Of course.

1161
01:12:06,322 --> 01:12:08,791
You may take it
as our company's consensus.

1162
01:12:10,626 --> 01:12:12,394
We take pride

1163
01:12:12,461 --> 01:12:14,363
in having run alongside

1164
01:12:14,430 --> 01:12:17,599
this broadcast since the first one.

1165
01:12:19,101 --> 01:12:23,105
We hope Dainichi TV
will keep airing the proud,

1166
01:12:23,172 --> 01:12:25,407
passionate Hakone Ekiden.

1167
01:12:26,608 --> 01:12:28,544
That is Miyako Beer's wish.

1168
01:12:30,546 --> 01:12:33,782
Thank you for your consideration.

1169
01:12:39,555 --> 01:12:42,191
Thank you, Mr. Sone.

1170
01:12:42,758 --> 01:12:43,759
Mr. Tokushige,

1171
01:12:44,827 --> 01:12:46,829
I'm looking forward to the next Hakone.

1172
01:12:49,398 --> 01:12:52,000
Goodbye.

1173
01:12:57,539 --> 01:12:59,308
As you just saw,

1174
01:13:00,142 --> 01:13:03,245
it's not just the runners and staff.

1175
01:13:04,380 --> 01:13:06,115
The sponsors are passionate too.

1176
01:13:07,383 --> 01:13:10,919
That's the Hakone Ekiden.

1177
01:13:16,692 --> 01:13:19,027
I see. That's enough.

1178
01:13:19,094 --> 01:13:22,998
Programming jumped the gun this time.

1179
01:13:24,700 --> 01:13:27,569
Wasn't there a lack of communication
with the staff?

1180
01:13:30,139 --> 01:13:35,411
Once President Tamura agrees to appear,

1181
01:13:35,477 --> 01:13:37,679
he won't back down quietly.

1182
01:13:39,181 --> 01:13:42,818
We need to stay
on good terms with Tamuken Pro.

1183
01:13:44,153 --> 01:13:46,155
So, Kuroishi,

1184
01:13:48,891 --> 01:13:52,861
cleaning up this mess is on you.

1185
01:13:53,595 --> 01:13:54,430
Understood?

1186
01:13:57,266 --> 01:13:58,600
Understood.

1187
01:14:02,304 --> 01:14:03,272
Good work.

1188
01:14:04,106 --> 01:14:07,709
Keep it up and make it
a great broadcast worthy of Hakone.

1189
01:14:10,479 --> 01:14:11,346
Yes!

1190
01:14:15,984 --> 01:14:16,819
-Huh?
-Huh?

1191
01:14:16,885 --> 01:14:17,886
Really?

1192
01:14:18,887 --> 01:14:20,289
‎At the executive meeting,

1193
01:14:23,158 --> 01:14:25,961
‎they gave the green light

1194
01:14:26,462 --> 01:14:28,163
‎for a great Hakone broadcast.

1195
01:14:28,230 --> 01:14:30,766
So don't worry

1196
01:14:30,833 --> 01:14:32,801
and get back to work!

1197
01:14:33,602 --> 01:14:35,337
-Yeah!
-Thank goodness!

1198
01:14:36,371 --> 01:14:40,209
Yeah!

1199
01:14:41,343 --> 01:14:42,911
Yeah!

1200
01:14:48,851 --> 01:14:51,487
-Cheers!
-Cheers!

1201
01:14:54,389 --> 01:14:57,025
I'm so glad!

1202
01:14:57,092 --> 01:14:59,695
I was sure
you were going to be transferred.

1203
01:14:59,761 --> 01:15:01,797
Don't say that so casually.

1204
01:15:01,864 --> 01:15:04,399
I didn't know you knew
someone at Miyako Beer.

1205
01:15:05,601 --> 01:15:07,469
You mean Mr. Sone, the sales director?

1206
01:15:07,536 --> 01:15:11,039
He ran track all through school.

1207
01:15:11,106 --> 01:15:13,475
Hakone means a lot to him.

1208
01:15:14,109 --> 01:15:15,010
He'd get fired up about it when drunk.

1209
01:15:15,077 --> 01:15:17,346
I was surprised Miyako Beer
backed us so completely.

1210
01:15:17,412 --> 01:15:20,382
They haven't been Hakone's main sponsor

1211
01:15:20,449 --> 01:15:23,986
for nearly 40 years for nothing.

1212
01:15:24,052 --> 01:15:25,754
Right.

1213
01:15:25,821 --> 01:15:29,091
So many people have kept Hakone going.

1214
01:15:29,157 --> 01:15:31,159
Oh, a rare good line from you.

1215
01:15:31,226 --> 01:15:32,594
What do you mean, rare?

1216
01:15:32,661 --> 01:15:36,098
Didn't you want Mr. Hatakeyama on?

1217
01:15:37,366 --> 01:15:40,035
Now, now. Have a drink.

1218
01:15:40,102 --> 01:15:42,504
But isn't it great?

1219
01:15:42,571 --> 01:15:44,706
At least we avoided
a crazy variety makeover.

1220
01:15:46,041 --> 01:15:47,409
Yeah.

1221
01:15:47,476 --> 01:15:51,513
But changing with the times
is one option too.

1222
01:15:53,448 --> 01:15:55,083
By the way, did you all know?

1223
01:15:55,150 --> 01:15:57,819
Natsuki's hooked on variety shows lately.

1224
01:15:57,886 --> 01:15:59,922
-Hey.
-You've been watching

1225
01:15:59,988 --> 01:16:01,790
all the old episodes of Laugh to Death,
right?

1226
01:16:01,857 --> 01:16:03,225
What?

1227
01:16:03,292 --> 01:16:04,793
That's an edgy pick.

1228
01:16:04,860 --> 01:16:07,396
-So? How was it?
-Huh?

1229
01:16:07,462 --> 01:16:08,997
What do you think of it?

1230
01:16:12,968 --> 01:16:14,036
It's not funny at all.

1231
01:16:15,871 --> 01:16:17,873
Actually, I don't really know

1232
01:16:17,940 --> 01:16:19,942
where I'm supposed to laugh.

1233
01:16:20,008 --> 01:16:21,209
So I'm analyzing it.

1234
01:16:21,276 --> 01:16:22,878
-Analyzing?
-Yes.

1235
01:16:22,945 --> 01:16:25,547
Last night
was the "Layered Underwear Championship."

1236
01:16:25,614 --> 01:16:27,049
Why wear layers of underwear?

1237
01:16:27,115 --> 01:16:30,586
And why is it funny
when you wear layers of underwear?

1238
01:16:30,652 --> 01:16:32,521
Aren't you overdoing it a bit?

1239
01:16:32,588 --> 01:16:33,922
Forget the underwear.

1240
01:16:33,989 --> 01:16:36,592
I'd rather you focus
completely on Hakone right now.

1241
01:16:36,658 --> 01:16:37,693
Of course.

1242
01:16:42,764 --> 01:16:45,167
Now it sounds like
I said something strange.

1243
01:16:47,636 --> 01:16:49,571
TOHO UNIVERSITY OF ECONOMICS
STUDENT UNITED TEAM

1244
01:16:49,638 --> 01:16:51,006
MEETING DAY

1245
01:16:51,073 --> 01:16:52,007
TOHO UNIVERSITY OF ECONOMICS
TRACK AND FIELD TEAM

1246
01:16:52,074 --> 01:16:55,277
What is the purpose
of this Student United Team?

1247
01:16:55,877 --> 01:16:58,981
We first need to make that clear.

1248
01:17:02,050 --> 01:17:03,552
My goal is a top-three finish

1249
01:17:04,753 --> 01:17:06,555
at the Hakone Ekiden.

1250
01:18:30,739 --> 01:18:31,973
‎I'm the only one who can go.

1251
01:18:32,040 --> 01:18:33,742
‎56 DAYS UNTIL HAKONE EKIDEN

1252
01:18:33,809 --> 01:18:34,910
‎THIS DRAMA IS A WORK OF FICTION
‎BASED ON THE HAKONE EKIDEN.

1253
01:18:34,976 --> 01:18:35,977
‎ALL PEOPLE AND ORGANIZATIONS DEPICTED
‎ARE UNRELATED TO REAL ONES.

1254
01:18:36,044 --> 01:18:36,978
‎STUDENT ACTIVITIES AND RULES IN THIS DRAMA
‎ARE FICTIONAL AND DON'T REFLECT REALITY.

1255
01:18:37,045 --> 01:18:38,013
‎Subtitle translation by: Ken Nishizaki
